{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794593455097,"sessionID":"ses_e29e5c0b9ffed1u4GCgcaPeWZq","part":{"partID":"prt_1d61afa7e002tw0GW6oY8yVEaA","sessionID":"ses_e29e5c0b9ffed1u4GCgcaPeWZq","messageID":"msg_1d61ae3860010jDGUp5kU4IsFt","type":"tool","id":"call_8eb9c6b939784d7da952a8ef","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"sed -n '120,320p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/tasks.md"},"output":"- [x] T030 [P] Cite the catalog's schema and handler anchors by name (`ARM`). Replace `` `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:308` `` with ``the `compiledRoute` field of `AdvisorRecommendationSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` ``, `` `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:310` `` with ``the `command` field of `AdvisorRecommendationSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` ``, `` `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:563-565`, `632-634` `` with ``the two `input.options?.includeCompiledRoute === false` checks in `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` ``, and each of `` `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:287` `` and `` `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:290` `` with ``the `options` of `AdvisorRecommendInputSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` ``. Leave the citations of `lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts`, `tools/advisor-recommend.ts` and `skill-advisor-cli-manifest.ts`. Verify: `rg -c \"advisor-tool-schemas\\.ts:[0-9]|handlers/advisor-recommend\\.ts:[0-9]\" $ARM` prints nothing, `rg -c \"AdvisorRecommendationSchema\" $ARM` prints 3, `rg -c \"AdvisorRecommendInputSchema\" $ARM` prints 2 and `bash $PL/probe-catalog-lines.sh` prints no `advisor-tool-schemas.ts` and no `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` line.\n\n### Wave 1, lane WG8: doctor embed and setup contracts\n- [x] T031 [P] Give a failed restore its own exit-3 outcome (`DAE`, `DAC`). Test first: in `DAC`, add `test('the embed workflow reads a failed restore as a partly written tree')`, which takes the one line of `EMBED_YAML` that contains `Exit 3 means` and asserts it matches `/ERROR: the restore failed/`, `/quote both ERROR lines/` and `/takes precedence over the restored: outcome/`. Run `NT $DAC` and see it fail on the first pattern. Then in `DAE`, inside the same quoted string that starts `Exit 3 means a write failed after the backup.`, append `When it holds ERROR: the restore failed, the restore itself threw and the tree may be partly written: quote both ERROR lines, show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and name the undo command as the next step. This outcome takes precedence over the restored: outcome.` Verify: the first run fails as described, then `NT $DAC` reports `fail 0`, `RV` exits 0 and `bash $PL/probe-embed-contract.sh` prints `workflow names the restore failure: 1`.\n- [x] T032 [P] Name the backup folder by the plan digest (`DAE`, `RTS`, `DAC`). Test first: in `DAC`, add `test('the embed workflow and route name the backup folder the engine makes')`, asserting that `EMBED_YAML` and `routeFor('embed').gate3_location` each contain `doctor-agents-md/<first 16 characters of the plan digest>/` and not `<timestamp>`, and that the route text contains `temporary directory`. Run `NT $DAC` and see it fail on `<timestamp>`. Then in `DAE` replace `.skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<timestamp>/` with `.skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<first 16 characters of the plan digest>/`, and in `RTS`, inside the embed route's `gate3_location`, replace `taken to the plan's backup folder under .skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<timestamp>/ before the first byte` with `taken to the plan's backup folder, .skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<first 16 characters of the plan digest>/ or the folder of that name under the operating system's temporary directory when git does not ignore that path, before the first byte`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `NT $DAC` reports `fail 0`, `RV` exits 0, `DERIVE` prints `{\"status\":\"fresh\",\"changed\":[]}` and `bash $PL/probe-embed-contract.sh` prints `route names the temporary-directory fallback: yes`.\n- [x] T033 [P] Give the setup router the workflow's reason for absent hook health (`DSM`, `DSCT`). Test first: in `DSCT`, inside `test('the setup workflow and router both name the unrecorded hook health state'`, add `assert.match(SETUP_ROUTER, /because no prompt hook has written a record for this checkout yet/)` and `assert.doesNotMatch(SETUP_ROUTER, /SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG/)`. Run `NT $DSCT` and see it fail on the first assertion. Then in `DSM` replace ``When the daemon holds no hook health records, the leg prints hook health not recorded and names `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG`, the setting that turns the records on.`` with `When the daemon holds no hook health records, the leg prints hook health not recorded, because no prompt hook has written a record for this checkout yet: OpenCode has no prompt hook that writes one and an unapproved Codex hook never runs.` Verify: the first run fails as described, then `NT $DSCT` reports `fail 0` and `RV` and `SRM` exit 0.\n\n### Wave 1, lane WG9: doctor check scripts\n- [x] T034 [P] Read a hook command the way a shell runs it (`HW`, `HWT`). Test first: in `HWT`, add one `test` per launch that writes `writeClaudeSettings(f.root, { UserPromptSubmit: [{ hooks: [{ type: 'command', command }] }] })` and expects exit 0 and `ok claude`, for the commands `` `env node ${CLAUDE_MARKER}` ``, `` `/usr/bin/env node ${CLAUDE_MARKER}` ``, `` `bash -lc \"node ${CLAUDE_MARKER}\"` ``, `` `zsh -c 'node ${CLAUDE_MARKER}'` ``, `` `node --no-warnings ${CLAUDE_MARKER}` ``, `` `cd \"$PWD\"&& node ${CLAUDE_MARKER}` `` and `` `cd /tmp; node ${CLAUDE_MARKER}` ``, and one more that expects exit 1 and `hook-missing claude .claude/settings.json` for `` `echo \"x && node ${CLAUDE_MARKER}\"` ``. Run `NT $HWT` and see the seven launches print `hook-missing` and the `echo` case print `ok`. Then in `HW` replace `stripQuotes`, `startsCommand` and the body of `runsMarker(command, marker)` with a reader that splits the command into words outside quotes, honouring single quotes, double quotes and a backslash escape, and ends a simple command at `&&`, `||`, `;`, `|` or a newline outside quotes, even one stuck to a word. A simple command is wired when, after any leading `NAME=value` words, its first word is `node` or a path ending `/node` and its first word after any words starting `-` ends with the marker. A first word of `env` or a path ending `/env` is dropped with the `NAME=value` and `-` words after it before that test. A first word of `bash`, `sh` or `zsh`, or a path ending in one, followed by a word that starts with a single `-` and holds `c`, makes the word after it a script that is read again as commands, at most two levels deep. A quoted word is otherwise only an argument, so an `echo` of a quoted script stays unwired. Keep the comment saying a mention is not a wired hook. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `NT $HWT` reports `fail 0` with every existing case unchanged, `node $HW --root .` prints `ok claude`, `ok codex`, `ok cursor` and `ok devin`, and `node $PL/probe-hook-shapes.cjs` prints `exit 0 ok claude` on each of its nine launch lines and `exit 1 hook-missing` on both `echo` lines.\n- [x] T035 [P] Count only verified copies as expected in A10 (`CHK`, `CHKT`). Test first: in `CHKT`, in the case `A10 leaves a missing pointer out of the count and names it after the copies`, replace the assertion that the detail matches `/^5\\/6 copies as expected/u` with `assert.equal(copies.detail, '3/6 copies as expected, 2 reported only, 1 pointer missing', ...)`. Run `NT $CHKT` and see it print `5/6 copies as expected, 1 pointer missing`. Then in `CHK`'s `rowRuntimeCopies`, count as expected only the entries whose `state` is `PASS`, count as reported only the `INFO` entries whose `kind` is not `pointer missing`, and build the detail as `<expected>/<total> copies as expected` followed by `, <n> unmeasured`, `, <n> reported only` and `, <n> pointer missing`, each only when its count is above 0. Leave the row's state rule as it is. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `NT $CHKT` reports `fail 0` and `A10Q` prints a detail whose first number equals its `pass` count and whose `reported only` number equals its `reported` count, which reads `3/6 copies as expected, 2 reported only, 1 pointer missing | pass 3 | reported 2` while the manifest holds the six entries it held at planning.\n\n### Wave 1, coordinator: the parent phase map\n- [x] T036 [C] Correct three rows of the parent phase map (`PS`). Re-read `PS` and the status rows of the 007, 014 and 015 child specs first. In row 7, after `(R8 transcripts, G2, G5)` add `. It stays open until the final behaviour arm, run on fresh arenas after the merge to main by operator instruction of 2026-11-13, settles T020, T046 and the acceptance rows AC-004, AC-005 and AC-007`. Set the Status cell of rows 14 and 15 to `Complete`. Change no other row. Verify: `bash $PL/probe-phase-map.sh | rg -e '^row (7|14|15) ' | rg -c differs` prints nothing and `rg -c \"until the final behaviour arm\" $PS` prints 1.\n\n### Verifier follow-ups, coordinator\nTwo independent verifiers read the wave 1 diff (`$SP/verify-wg1-4.md`, `$SP/verify-wg5-9.md`): 33 of 33 tasks do what their line says, no P0 or P1 and nine P2. The four below were built by the coordinator. Four were left: the g2 run-line write in `R` has no suite test and stays covered by `$PL/probe-arm-fixture.mjs`, which T039 reruns. The literal marker path in `trustedCheckout` agrees with the arena builder and fails toward untrusted. A busy code split across two writes now counts as busy, which is a busy variant. The catalog pages of four other skills that name `metadata.compiledRouteSummary` belong to other skills and the advisor's hook path still carries that field, so they are outside this phase.\n- [x] T042 [C] Narrow the no-edit pattern so a change request that limits its scope keeps its command (`CA`, `CAG`). The bare `no changes` alternative read `refactor the parser so there are no changes to its public api` as a no-edit request. Replace it with `make no changes|no changes yet` and add an `it.each` of three scope-limiting change requests expecting `isNoEditRequest` to be `false`. Verify: `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, `VX tests/scorer/read-only-explainer.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` report 0 failed and `rg -c \"make no changes\\|no changes yet\" $CA` prints 1.\n- [x] T043 [C] End the `--row-id` sentence before `--json` (`RA`). Verify: ``rg -c 'usage error with `--runtime`\\. `--json` prints' $RA`` prints 1.\n- [x] T044 [C] Read the launch shapes the first reader got wrong (`HW`, `HWT`). Test first: seven launches a shell runs (`env -u NAME`, `node -r`, a subshell, a brace group, `exec`, a background command first and a backslash line continuation) expecting `ok claude`, and five that run nothing (an unclosed quote, `node --check`, `node -e`, a launch inside a comment and a shell script that takes its own `-c`) expecting `hook-missing`. Nine of the twelve failed before the change. Verify: `NT $HWT` reports `fail 0` with 28 passed, `node $HW --root .` prints `ok claude`, `ok codex`, `ok cursor` and `ok devin` and `node $PL/probe-hook-shapes.cjs` prints the lines T034 names.\n- [x] T045 [C] Make the plugin field test fail on a dropped owner (`PJT`). The row's owner equalled its skill id, so the label did not change when the owner was dropped. Give the row the skill id `system-spec-kit` and keep the owner `sk-doc`. Verify: `VP` reports `fail 0`, and a copy of the test with the `ownerSkillId` line removed reports `fail 1`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [x] T037 [C] Rebuild and run every suite (`$SP/after.txt`). Run `npm run build` in `ADV`, `TC`, `VALL`, `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1 npx vitest run tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts` in `ADV`, `DALL`, `VSR`, `VP`, `DERIVE`, `RV`, `SRM` and `PBV`, and write each command with its result lines into `after.txt`. Verify: the build, `TC`, `RV` and `SRM` exit 0, `VALL` reports 0 failed with more passed tests than `$SP/before.txt`, the child-flag run reports 0 failed, `DALL`, `VSR` and `VP` report `fail 0`, `DERIVE` prints `{\"status\":\"fresh\",\"changed\":[]}` and `PBV` prints its `PASS` line.\n- [x] T038 [C] Hold every floor equal (`$SP/after.txt`). Run `FLOOR`, `EVAL` and `A10Q`, write each beside its `before.txt` line and end the file with `RESULT: every floor equals its before line` only when each `FLOOR` and `EVAL` line does. When one differs, write the difference, mark this task `[B]` and do not tune a pattern to restore it. Verify: each of the four `FLOOR` lines and the `EVAL` line equals its `before.txt` line character for character, and `rg -c \"^RESULT: every floor equals its before line$\" $SP/after.txt` prints 1.\n- [x] T039 [C] Rerun the reproductions (`$SP/repro-after.txt`). Run the 18 probes in `PL` after the build, as T002 did, and write their output. Verify: `rg -cF -e 'attach \"make no changes\" -> undefined' -e 'scorer commandMeaningEligible \"make no changes\" -> false' -e 'fake CLI ran: false, fake hook ran: false' -e 'left on disk: notes draft.md false, plain.md false' -e '--row-id g2-deep-review-ask -> arm g2' -e 'arm refused mixed_row_arms' -e 'run line records the fixture: true' -e 'variables left changed: []' -e 'hook saw AI_SESSION_CHILD=<unset>' -e 'marker after 1 MiB: errorCode SQLITE_BUSY_EXHAUSTED, retriesAttempted 1' -e 'bash -lc: exit 0 ok claude' -e 'echo with a quoted script: exit 1 hook-missing' -e 'workflow names the restore failure: 1' -e 'route names the temporary-directory fallback: yes' -e 'privacy case persists a record: true' -e 'LF: raw break in literal false, parses true' -e 'plugin test asserts a command label: true' -e 'compiledRouteSummary lines: []' -e 'stdout= stderr=score-command-transcripts.mjs: --row-id narrows --summary only' $SP/repro-after.txt` prints 19.\n- [x] T040 [C] Check the boundaries. Verify: `G diff --quiet BASE -- AGENTS.md` exits 0, `G diff --stat BASE -- '*package.json' '*package-lock.json'` prints nothing, `G diff BASE -U0 -- .skilled .opencode | rg \"^\\+.*(//|#|\\*).*(specs/|REQ-0|ADR-0|T0[0-9]{2}|phase [0-9]|WG[0-9]|DR[0-9]-P|SA[0-9]-P|iter[0-9]-P)\"` prints nothing, the same `rg` over `$ADV/tests/derive-command-bridges-strings.vitest.ts` prints nothing, `G diff BASE -U0 -- .skilled .opencode | rg -c \"^\\+.*/create:(sk-)?skill\\b\"` prints nothing, `G diff --name-only BASE -- .skilled .opencode` together with the untracked files in `G status --short -- .skilled .opencode` names only files that T003 to T035 name, and `G diff BASE -U0 -- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md | rg -c '^\\+\\| (7|14|15) \\|'` prints 3.\n- [x] T041 [C] Close out (`implementation-summary.md`, `acceptance-criteria.md`). Write the summary from `$SP/after.txt` and `$SP/repro-after.txt`, mark each acceptance row with the evidence observed, run `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/repair-derived.cjs --folder <this folder> --apply` and then strict validation. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <this folder> --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [x] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [x] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [x] `$SP/after.txt` ends `RESULT: every floor equals its before line` and `$SP/repro-after.txt` holds every fixed output T039 names\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Acceptance criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n- **Review report**: `../review/review-report.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n## Verification Protocol\n\n| Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n|----------|----------|-------------------|\n| **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n| **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n| **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n\nA blocked task gets `[B]` and one line naming what blocks it. A floor that moves blocks the phase.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n## Pre-Implementation\n\n- [x] CHK-001 [P0] Phase 016 is committed, and the before numbers and the reproductions are in `scratch/` (T001, T002). Evidence: `scratch/before.txt` shows the `log` printing `ec1869dae8`, `test -e` `exit=1` and an empty status, and `scratch/repro-before.txt` holds 18 probes, each `exit=0`, with the T002 count printing 17.\n- [x] CHK-002 [P0] Each task line ends with a verify clause: `rg -c '^- \\[[ xB]\\] T[0-9].*Verify: ' tasks.md` and `rg -c '^- \\[[ xB]\\] T[0-9]' tasks.md` print the same number. Evidence: both print 45 at close-out.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n## Code Quality\n\n- [x] CHK-010 [P0] `TC` exits 0 and `node --check` passes on every changed `.mjs`, `.cjs` and `.js` file. Evidence: `scratch/after.txt` `TC` `exit=0`, and the close-out `node --check` exits 0 on all 15 changed script files.\n- [x] CHK-011 [P0] No code comment names a spec path, a phase number, a task id, a finding id, an ADR or a REQ id (T040). Evidence: the close-out rerun of the T040 label scan prints nothing on the diff against `ec1869dae8` and on the new test file.\n- [x] CHK-012 [P0] `CA` still has no import, so the scorer can import it without a cycle: `rg -c \"^import\" $CA` prints nothing. Evidence: the close-out rerun prints nothing and exits 1.\n- [x] CHK-013 [P1] The generated blocks in `CA` stay the deriver's own: `DERIVE` prints `{\"status\":\"fresh\",\"changed\":[]}` after T009 and after T032. Evidence: `scratch/after.txt` `DERIVE` prints `{\"status\":\"fresh\",\"changed\":[]}` on the final tree, which holds both changes.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## Testing Checklist\n\n- [x] CHK-020 [P0] Every floor equals its before line (T038). Evidence: `scratch/after.txt` ends `RESULT: every floor equals its before line`, and its four `FLOOR` lines and `[160,50,21,5]` equal `scratch/before.txt`.\n- [x] CHK-021 [P0] Each fix's verify recorded its test failing before the change and passing after, except the cases the spec names as passing today. Evidence: the `scratch/logs/` report of each of the 20 test-first tasks (T003 to T005, T008 to T016, T022, T023, T029, T031 to T035) records its red run, T044 records nine of twelve new cases failing first, and T042's three cases match verifier finding F1, whose probe read those prompts as no-edit before the change.\n- [x] CHK-022 [P0] The planning probes print the fixed outputs (T039). Evidence: the T039 count on `scratch/repro-after.txt` prints 19, and all 18 probes record `exit=0`.\n- [x] CHK-023 [P1] The fallback envelope test passes under `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` (T037). Evidence: the `child-flag envelope` run in `scratch/after.txt` reads `Tests 4 passed (4)`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n## FIX ADDENDUM: FIX COMPLETENESS\n\n- [x] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Each finding has a class: the no-edit gate `cross-consumer` (attach path, two scorer gates, explainer), the backfill trust and the busy scan `algorithmic`, the quoted restore and the launch reader `class-of-bug` (every quoted path and every wrapper shape), the arm label and the replayed fixture `instance-only`, the two measurement scripts `test-isolation`, and the doc, comment and contract findings `instance-only`. Evidence: the cross-consumer fix reaches all four consumers, `command-attach.ts:335`, `fusion.ts:677` and `:881` and `text.ts:150`, and the restore reads every path through `status --porcelain -z`.\n- [x] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Same-class producers: `rg -ln \"without making changes\" .skilled --glob '!**/node_modules/**' --glob '!**/dist/**'` lists no code file after T004. Evidence: the close-out rerun no longer lists `scorer/text.ts`. Its two code hits are the shared pattern itself in `command-attach.ts` and a `--dry-run` help string in `mcp-code-mode/scripts/install.sh`, which is not a copy of the pattern.\n- [x] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Consumers of every changed symbol are the ones `plan.md` lists, and the consumer `rg` in its required inventories prints no unlisted file. Evidence: the close-out rerun lists `command-attach.ts`, `scorer/text.ts` and `fusion.ts` lines 20, 36, 677, 709, 717, 881 and 1236, `backfillRunLog` only in `command-offer.vitest.ts` and `copies as expected` only in `agents-md-check.cjs` and its test.\n- [x] CHK-FIX-004 [P0] The path, parser and trust fixes carry adversarial cases: a file name with a space, a rename to a name with a space, a checkout with fake code and no marker, a marker inside a quoted `echo` argument and a marker named only in a `description` field. Evidence: `worktree-restore.vitest.ts` and `command-offer.vitest.ts` hold the first three, and `hook-wiring-check.test.cjs` holds `names a runtime whose entry echoes a quoted command` and `names a runtime whose entry only describes the script`.\n- [x] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] The matrix rows `plan.md` lists for the no-edit gate and the launch reader each exist in the tests T003 to T005 and T034 add. Evidence: the four wordings run on `attachCommand` and on `isReadOnlyExplainer`, the curly wording runs on `commandMeaningEligible`, and `hook-wiring-check.test.cjs` holds `node`, `env`, `/usr/bin/env`, `bash -lc`, `zsh -c`, a flag, a stuck separator and a quoted `echo`. `sh` has no case of its own and shares one list with `bash` and `zsh` at `hook-wiring-check.cjs:241`.\n- [x] CHK-FIX-006 [P1] The hostile environment variants ran: the cost script with `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` in its parent and the capture compared against a snapshot of the caller's environment. Evidence: `scratch/repro-after.txt` prints `hook saw AI_SESSION_CHILD=<unset>` and `variables left changed: []`, and the T014 and T015 cases pass in `VALL`.\n- [x] CHK-FIX-007 [P1] Evidence names the commit it ran on: `scratch/after.txt` and `implementation-summary.md` name the base commit with the changes in the working tree. Evidence: `scratch/after.txt` reads `base ec1869dae8 with the changes in the working tree`, and the summary's Metadata names `ec1869dae8`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n## Security\n\n- [x] CHK-030 [P0] No task prints holdout prompt text or opens `holdout-prompts.jsonl`. Evidence: none of the 673 worker tool calls in `scratch/logs/` names `holdout-prompts`, and the coordinator commands in `scratch/before.txt` and `scratch/after.txt` name no holdout file.\n- [x] CHK-031 [P0] No task starts a model session, runs a live arm, approves a Codex hook or writes under the home folder. Evidence: none of the 673 worker tool calls names a model CLI or a home path, and the coordinator records hold no live arm or hook approval.\n- [x] CHK-032 [P0] The backfill spawns nothing from an untrusted checkout (T010). Evidence: `scratch/repro-after.txt` prints `fake CLI ran: false, fake hook ran: false`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n## Documentation\n\n- [x] CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `acceptance-criteria.md` state the same names, floors and fixed outputs. Evidence: `spec.md` REQ-001 now names `make no changes` and `no changes yet`, as T042 built them.\n- [x] CHK-041 [P1] The README, playbook, catalog, workflow and router edits match the code (T008, T017 to T024, T030 to T033): each verify prints what it says on the final tree. Evidence: the close-out `rg` reruns of T008, T017 to T021, T024 and T030 print what their lines name, `PBV` prints its `PASS` line, `DALL` reads `fail 0` and `scratch/repro-after.txt` prints the T031 to T033 probe lines.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n## File Organization\n\n- [x] CHK-050 [P1] The before and after records and the reproductions live in `scratch/` only, and no temporary probe or test folder remains. Evidence: the records are in `scratch/` only, and the `advisor-status` suite now removes every temporary tree it makes: a run of that file left the count of `advisor-status-*` folders in the system temp folder unchanged.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## Verification Summary\n\n| Category | Total | Verified |\n|----------|-------|----------|\n| P0 Items | 15 | 15/15 |\n| P1 Items | 8 | 8/8 |\n| P2 Items | 0 | 0/0 |\n\n**Verification Date**: 2026-11-13\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"- [x] T030 [P] Cite the catalog's schema and handler anchors by name (`ARM`). Replace `` `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:308` `` with ``the `compiledRoute` field of `AdvisorRecommendationSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` ``, `` `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:310` `` with ``the `command` field of `AdvisorRecommendationSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` ``, `` `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:563-565`, `632-634` `` with ``the two `input.options?.includeCompiledRoute === false` checks in `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` ``, and each of `` `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:287` `` and `` `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:290` `` with ``the `options` of `AdvisorRecommendInputSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` ``. Leave the citations of `lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts`, `tools/advisor-recommend.ts` and `skill-advisor-cli-manifest.ts`. Verify: `rg -c \"advisor-tool-schemas\\.ts:[0-9]|handlers/advisor-recommend\\.ts:[0-9]\" $ARM` prints nothing, `rg -c \"AdvisorRecommendationSchema\" $ARM` prints 3, `rg -c \"AdvisorRecommendInputSchema\" $ARM` prints 2 and `bash $PL/probe-catalog-lines.sh` prints no `advisor-tool-schemas.ts` and no `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` line.\n\n### Wave 1, lane WG8: doctor embed and setup contracts\n- [x] T031 [P] Give a failed restore its own exit-3 outcome (`DAE`, `DAC`). Test first: in `DAC`, add `test('the embed workflow reads a failed restore as a partly written tree')`, which takes the one line of `EMBED_YAML` that contains `Exit 3 means` and asserts it matches `/ERROR: the restore failed/`, `/quote both ERROR lines/` and `/takes precedence over the restored: outcome/`. Run `NT $DAC` and see it fail on the first pattern. Then in `DAE`, inside the same quoted string that starts `Exit 3 means a write failed after the backup.`, append `When it holds ERROR: the restore failed, the restore itself threw and the tree may be partly written: quote both ERROR lines, show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and name the undo command as the next step. This outcome takes precedence over the restored: outcome.` Verify: the first run fails as described, then `NT $DAC` reports `fail 0`, `RV` exits 0 and `bash $PL/probe-embed-contract.sh` prints `workflow names the restore failure: 1`.\n- [x] T032 [P] Name the backup folder by the plan digest (`DAE`, `RTS`, `DAC`). Test first: in `DAC`, add `test('the embed workflow and route name the backup folder the engine makes')`, asserting that `EMBED_YAML` and `routeFor('embed').gate3_location` each contain `doctor-agents-md/<first 16 characters of the plan digest>/` and not `<timestamp>`, and that the route text contains `temporary directory`. Run `NT $DAC` and see it fail on `<timestamp>`. Then in `DAE` replace `.skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<timestamp>/` with `.skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<first 16 characters of the plan digest>/`, and in `RTS`, inside the embed route's `gate3_location`, replace `taken to the plan's backup folder under .skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<timestamp>/ before the first byte` with `taken to the plan's backup folder, .skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<first 16 characters of the plan digest>/ or the folder of that name under the operating system's temporary directory when git does not ignore that path, before the first byte`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `NT $DAC` reports `fail 0`, `RV` exits 0, `DERIVE` prints `{\"status\":\"fresh\",\"changed\":[]}` and `bash $PL/probe-embed-contract.sh` prints `route names the temporary-directory fallback: yes`.\n- [x] T033 [P] Give the setup router the workflow's reason for absent hook health (`DSM`, `DSCT`). Test first: in `DSCT`, inside `test('the setup workflow and router both name the unrecorded hook health state'`, add `assert.match(SETUP_ROUTER, /because no prompt hook has written a record for this checkout yet/)` and `assert.doesNotMatch(SETUP_ROUTER, /SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG/)`. Run `NT $DSCT` and see it fail on the first assertion. Then in `DSM` replace ``When the daemon holds no hook health records, the leg prints hook health not recorded and names `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG`, the setting that turns the records on.`` with `When the daemon holds no hook health records, the leg prints hook health not recorded, because no prompt hook has written a record for this checkout yet: OpenCode has no prompt hook that writes one and an unapproved Codex hook never runs.` Verify: the first run fails as described, then `NT $DSCT` reports `fail 0` and `RV` and `SRM` exit 0.\n\n### Wave 1, lane WG9: doctor check scripts\n- [x] T034 [P] Read a hook command the way a shell runs it (`HW`, `HWT`). Test first: in `HWT`, add one `test` per launch that writes `writeClaudeSettings(f.root, { UserPromptSubmit: [{ hooks: [{ type: 'command', command }] }] })` and expects exit 0 and `ok claude`, for the commands `` `env node ${CLAUDE_MARKER}` ``, `` `/usr/bin/env node ${CLAUDE_MARKER}` ``, `` `bash -lc \"node ${CLAUDE_MARKER}\"` ``, `` `zsh -c 'node ${CLAUDE_MARKER}'` ``, `` `node --no-warnings ${CLAUDE_MARKER}` ``, `` `cd \"$PWD\"&& node ${CLAUDE_MARKER}` `` and `` `cd /tmp; node ${CLAUDE_MARKER}` ``, and one more that expects exit 1 and `hook-missing claude .claude/settings.json` for `` `echo \"x && node ${CLAUDE_MARKER}\"` ``. Run `NT $HWT` and see the seven launches print `hook-missing` and the `echo` case print `ok`. Then in `HW` replace `stripQuotes`, `startsCommand` and the body of `runsMarker(command, marker)` with a reader that splits the command into words outside quotes, honouring single quotes, double quotes and a backslash escape, and ends a simple command at `&&`, `||`, `;`, `|` or a newline outside quotes, even one stuck to a word. A simple command is wired when, after any leading `NAME=value` words, its first word is `node` or a path ending `/node` and its first word after any words starting `-` ends with the marker. A first word of `env` or a path ending `/env` is dropped with the `NAME=value` and `-` words after it before that test. A first word of `bash`, `sh` or `zsh`, or a path ending in one, followed by a word that starts with a single `-` and holds `c`, makes the word after it a script that is read again as commands, at most two levels deep. A quoted word is otherwise only an argument, so an `echo` of a quoted script stays unwired. Keep the comment saying a mention is not a wired hook. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `NT $HWT` reports `fail 0` with every existing case unchanged, `node $HW --root .` prints `ok claude`, `ok codex`, `ok cursor` and `ok devin`, and `node $PL/probe-hook-shapes.cjs` prints `exit 0 ok claude` on each of its nine launch lines and `exit 1 hook-missing` on both `echo` lines.\n- [x] T035 [P] Count only verified copies as expected in A10 (`CHK`, `CHKT`). Test first: in `CHKT`, in the case `A10 leaves a missing pointer out of the count and names it after the copies`, replace the assertion that the detail matches `/^5\\/6 copies as expected/u` with `assert.equal(copies.detail, '3/6 copies as expected, 2 reported only, 1 pointer missing', ...)`. Run `NT $CHKT` and see it print `5/6 copies as expected, 1 pointer missing`. Then in `CHK`'s `rowRuntimeCopies`, count as expected only the entries whose `state` is `PASS`, count as reported only the `INFO` entries whose `kind` is not `pointer missing`, and build the detail as `<expected>/<total> copies as expected` followed by `, <n> unmeasured`, `, <n> reported only` and `, <n> pointer missing`, each only when its count is above 0. Leave the row's state rule as it is. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `NT $CHKT` reports `fail 0` and `A10Q` prints a detail whose first number equals its `pass` count and whose `reported only` number equals its `reported` count, which reads `3/6 copies as expected, 2 reported only, 1 pointer missing | pass 3 | reported 2` while the manifest holds the six entries it held at planning.\n\n### Wave 1, coordinator: the parent phase map\n- [x] T036 [C] Correct three rows of the parent phase map (`PS`). Re-read `PS` and the status rows of the 007, 014 and 015 child specs first. In row 7, after `(R8 transcripts, G2, G5)` add `. It stays open until the final behaviour arm, run on fresh arenas after the merge to main by operator instruction of 2026-11-13, settles T020, T046 and the acceptance rows AC-004, AC-005 and AC-007`. Set the Status cell of rows 14 and 15 to `Complete`. Change no other row. Verify: `bash $PL/probe-phase-map.sh | rg -e '^row (7|14|15) ' | rg -c differs` prints nothing and `rg -c \"until the final behaviour arm\" $PS` prints 1.\n\n### Verifier follow-ups, coordinator\nTwo independent verifiers read the wave 1 diff (`$SP/verify-wg1-4.md`, `$SP/verify-wg5-9.md`): 33 of 33 tasks do what their line says, no P0 or P1 and nine P2. The four below were built by the coordinator. Four were left: the g2 run-line write in `R` has no suite test and stays covered by `$PL/probe-arm-fixture.mjs`, which T039 reruns. The literal marker path in `trustedCheckout` agrees with the arena builder and fails toward untrusted. A busy code split across two writes now counts as busy, which is a busy variant. The catalog pages of four other skills that name `metadata.compiledRouteSummary` belong to other skills and the advisor's hook path still carries that field, so they are outside this phase.\n- [x] T042 [C] Narrow the no-edit pattern so a change request that limits its scope keeps its command (`CA`, `CAG`). The bare `no changes` alternative read `refactor the parser so there are no changes to its public api` as a no-edit request. Replace it with `make no changes|no changes yet` and add an `it.each` of three scope-limiting change requests expecting `isNoEditRequest` to be `false`. Verify: `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, `VX tests/scorer/read-only-explainer.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` report 0 failed and `rg -c \"make no changes\\|no changes yet\" $CA` prints 1.\n- [x] T043 [C] End the `--row-id` sentence before `--json` (`RA`). Verify: ``rg -c 'usage error with `--runtime`\\. `--json` prints' $RA`` prints 1.\n- [x] T044 [C] Read the launch shapes the first reader got wrong (`HW`, `HWT`). Test first: seven launches a shell runs (`env -u NAME`, `node -r`, a subshell, a brace group, `exec`, a background command first and a backslash line continuation) expecting `ok claude`, and five that run nothing (an unclosed quote, `node --check`, `node -e`, a launch inside a comment and a shell script that takes its own `-c`) expecting `hook-missing`. Nine of the twelve failed before the change. Verify: `NT $HWT` reports `fail 0` with 28 passed, `node $HW --root .` prints `ok claude`, `ok codex`, `ok cursor` and `ok devin` and `node $PL/probe-hook-shapes.cjs` prints the lines T034 names.\n- [x] T045 [C] Make the plugin field test fail on a dropped owner (`PJT`). The row's owner equalled its skill id, so the label did not change when the owner was dropped. Give the row the skill id `system-spec-kit` and keep the owner `sk-doc`. Verify: `VP` reports `fail 0`, and a copy of the test with the `ownerSkillId` line removed reports `fail 1`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [x] T037 [C] Rebuild and run every suite (`$SP/after.txt`). Run `npm run build` in `ADV`, `TC`, `VALL`, `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1 npx vitest run tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts` in `ADV`, `DALL`, `VSR`, `VP`, `DERIVE`, `RV`, `SRM` and `PBV`, and write each command with its result lines into `after.txt`. Verify: the build, `TC`, `RV` and `SRM` exit 0, `VALL` reports 0 failed with more passed tests than `$SP/before.txt`, the child-flag run reports 0 failed, `DALL`, `VSR` and `VP` report `fail 0`, `DERIVE` prints `{\"status\":\"fresh\",\"changed\":[]}` and `PBV` prints its `PASS` line.\n- [x] T038 [C] Hold every floor equal (`$SP/after.txt`). Run `FLOOR`, `EVAL` and `A10Q`, write each beside its `before.txt` line and end the file with `RESULT: every floor equals its before line` only when each `FLOOR` and `EVAL` line does. When one differs, write the difference, mark this task `[B]` and do not tune a pattern to restore it. Verify: each of the four `FLOOR` lines and the `EVAL` line equals its `before.txt` line character for character, and `rg -c \"^RESULT: every floor equals its before line$\" $SP/after.txt` prints 1.\n- [x] T039 [C] Rerun the reproductions (`$SP/repro-after.txt`). Run the 18 probes in `PL` after the build, as T002 did, and write their output. Verify: `rg -cF -e 'attach \"make no changes\" -> undefined' -e 'scorer commandMeaningEligible \"make no changes\" -> false' -e 'fake CLI ran: false, fake hook ran: false' -e 'left on disk: notes draft.md false, plain.md false' -e '--row-id g2-deep-review-ask -> arm g2' -e 'arm refused mixed_row_arms' -e 'run line records the fixture: true' -e 'variables left changed: []' -e 'hook saw AI_SESSION_CHILD=<unset>' -e 'marker after 1 MiB: errorCode SQLITE_BUSY_EXHAUSTED, retriesAttempted 1' -e 'bash -lc: exit 0 ok claude' -e 'echo with a quoted script: exit 1 hook-missing' -e 'workflow names the restore failure: 1' -e 'route names the temporary-directory fallback: yes' -e 'privacy case persists a record: true' -e 'LF: raw break in literal false, parses true' -e 'plugin test asserts a command label: true' -e 'compiledRouteSummary lines: []' -e 'stdout= stderr=score-command-transcripts.mjs: --row-id narrows --summary only' $SP/repro-after.txt` prints 19.\n- [x] T040 [C] Check the boundaries. Verify: `G diff --quiet BASE -- AGENTS.md` exits 0, `G diff --stat BASE -- '*package.json' '*package-lock.json'` prints nothing, `G diff BASE -U0 -- .skilled .opencode | rg \"^\\+.*(//|#|\\*).*(specs/|REQ-0|ADR-0|T0[0-9]{2}|phase [0-9]|WG[0-9]|DR[0-9]-P|SA[0-9]-P|iter[0-9]-P)\"` prints nothing, the same `rg` over `$ADV/tests/derive-command-bridges-strings.vitest.ts` prints nothing, `G diff BASE -U0 -- .skilled .opencode | rg -c \"^\\+.*/create:(sk-)?skill\\b\"` prints nothing, `G diff --name-only BASE -- .skilled .opencode` together with the untracked files in `G status --short -- .skilled .opencode` names only files that T003 to T035 name, and `G diff BASE -U0 -- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md | rg -c '^\\+\\| (7|14|15) \\|'` prints 3.\n- [x] T041 [C] Close out (`implementation-summary.md`, `acceptance-criteria.md`). Write the summary from `$SP/after.txt` and `$SP/repro-after.txt`, mark each acceptance row with the evidence observed, run `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/repair-derived.cjs --folder <this folder> --apply` and then strict validation. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <this folder> --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [x] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [x] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [x] `$SP/after.txt` ends `RESULT: every floor equals its before line` and `$SP/repro-after.txt` holds every fixed output T039 names\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Acceptance criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n- **Review report**: `../review/review-report.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n## Verification Protocol\n\n| Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n|----------|----------|-------------------|\n| **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n| **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n| **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n\nA blocked task gets `[B]` and one line naming what blocks it. A floor that moves blocks the phase.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n## Pre-Implementation\n\n- [x] CHK-001 [P0] Phase 016 is committed, and the before numbers and the reproductions are in `scratch/` (T001, T002). Evidence: `scratch/before.txt` shows the `log` printing `ec1869dae8`, `test -e` `exit=1` and an empty status, and `scratch/repro-before.txt` holds 18 probes, each `exit=0`, with the T002 count printing 17.\n- [x] CHK-002 [P0] Each task line ends with a verify clause: `rg -c '^- \\[[ xB]\\] T[0-9].*Verify: ' tasks.md` and `rg -c '^- \\[[ xB]\\] T[0-9]' tasks.md` print the same number. Evidence: both print 45 at close-out.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n## Code Quality\n\n- [x] CHK-010 [P0] `TC` exits 0 and `node --check` passes on every changed `.mjs`, `.cjs` and `.js` file. Evidence: `scratch/after.txt` `TC` `exit=0`, and the close-out `node --check` exits 0 on all 15 changed script files.\n- [x] CHK-011 [P0] No code comment names a spec path, a phase number, a task id, a finding id, an ADR or a REQ id (T040). Evidence: the close-out rerun of the T040 label scan prints nothing on the diff against `ec1869dae8` and on the new test file.\n- [x] CHK-012 [P0] `CA` still has no import, so the scorer can import it without a cycle: `rg -c \"^import\" $CA` prints nothing. Evidence: the close-out rerun prints nothing and exits 1.\n- [x] CHK-013 [P1] The generated blocks in `CA` stay the deriver's own: `DERIVE` prints `{\"status\":\"fresh\",\"changed\":[]}` after T009 and after T032. Evidence: `scratch/after.txt` `DERIVE` prints `{\"status\":\"fresh\",\"changed\":[]}` on the final tree, which holds both changes.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## Testing Checklist\n\n- [x] CHK-020 [P0] Every floor equals its before line (T038). Evidence: `scratch/after.txt` ends `RESULT: every floor equals its before line`, and its four `FLOOR` lines and `[160,50,21,5]` equal `scratch/before.txt`.\n- [x] CHK-021 [P0] Each fix's verify recorded its test failing before the change and passing after, except the cases the spec names as passing today. Evidence: the `scratch/logs/` report of each of the 20 test-first tasks (T003 to T005, T008 to T016, T022, T023, T029, T031 to T035) records its red run, T044 records nine of twelve new cases failing first, and T042's three cases match verifier finding F1, whose probe read those prompts as no-edit before the change.\n- [x] CHK-022 [P0] The planning probes print the fixed outputs (T039). Evidence: the T039 count on `scratch/repro-after.txt` prints 19, and all 18 probes record `exit=0`.\n- [x] CHK-023 [P1] The fallback envelope test passes under `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` (T037). Evidence: the `child-flag envelope` run in `scratch/after.txt` reads `Tests 4 passed (4)`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n## FIX ADDENDUM: FIX COMPLETENESS\n\n- [x] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Each finding has a class: the no-edit gate `cross-consumer` (attach path, two scorer gates, explainer), the backfill trust and the busy scan `algorithmic`, the quoted restore and the launch reader `class-of-bug` (every quoted path and every wrapper shape), the arm label and the replayed fixture `instance-only`, the two measurement scripts `test-isolation`, and the doc, comment and contract findings `instance-only`. Evidence: the cross-consumer fix reaches all four consumers, `command-attach.ts:335`, `fusion.ts:677` and `:881` and `text.ts:150`, and the restore reads every path through `status --porcelain -z`.\n- [x] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Same-class producers: `rg -ln \"without making changes\" .skilled --glob '!**/node_modules/**' --glob '!**/dist/**'` lists no code file after T004. Evidence: the close-out rerun no longer lists `scorer/text.ts`. Its two code hits are the shared pattern itself in `command-attach.ts` and a `--dry-run` help string in `mcp-code-mode/scripts/install.sh`, which is not a copy of the pattern.\n- [x] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Consumers of every changed symbol are the ones `plan.md` lists, and the consumer `rg` in its required inventories prints no unlisted file. Evidence: the close-out rerun lists `command-attach.ts`, `scorer/text.ts` and `fusion.ts` lines 20, 36, 677, 709, 717, 881 and 1236, `backfillRunLog` only in `command-offer.vitest.ts` and `copies as expected` only in `agents-md-check.cjs` and its test.\n- [x] CHK-FIX-004 [P0] The path, parser and trust fixes carry adversarial cases: a file name with a space, a rename to a name with a space, a checkout with fake code and no marker, a marker inside a quoted `echo` argument and a marker named only in a `description` field. Evidence: `worktree-restore.vitest.ts` and `command-offer.vitest.ts` hold the first three, and `hook-wiring-check.test.cjs` holds `names a runtime whose entry echoes a quoted command` and `names a runtime whose entry only describes the script`.\n- [x] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] The matrix rows `plan.md` lists for the no-edit gate and the launch reader each exist in the tests T003 to T005 and T034 add. Evidence: the four wordings run on `attachCommand` and on `isReadOnlyExplainer`, the curly wording runs on `commandMeaningEligible`, and `hook-wiring-check.test.cjs` holds `node`, `env`, `/usr/bin/env`, `bash -lc`, `zsh -c`, a flag, a stuck separator and a quoted `echo`. `sh` has no case of its own and shares one list with `bash` and `zsh` at `hook-wiring-check.cjs:241`.\n- [x] CHK-FIX-006 [P1] The hostile environment variants ran: the cost script with `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` in its parent and the capture compared against a snapshot of the caller's environment. Evidence: `scratch/repro-after.txt` prints `hook saw AI_SESSION_CHILD=<unset>` and `variables left changed: []`, and the T014 and T015 cases pass in `VALL`.\n- [x] CHK-FIX-007 [P1] Evidence names the commit it ran on: `scratch/after.txt` and `implementation-summary.md` name the base commit with the changes in the working tree. Evidence: `scratch/after.txt` reads `base ec1869dae8 with the changes in the working tree`, and the summary's Metadata names `ec1869dae8`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n## Security\n\n- [x] CHK-030 [P0] No task prints holdout prompt text or opens `holdout-prompts.jsonl`. Evidence: none of the 673 worker tool calls in `scratch/logs/` names `holdout-prompts`, and the coordinator commands in `scratch/before.txt` and `scratch/after.txt` name no holdout file.\n- [x] CHK-031 [P0] No task starts a model session, runs a live arm, approves a Codex hook or writes under the home folder. Evidence: none of the 673 worker tool calls names a model CLI or a home path, and the coordinator records hold no live arm or hook approval.\n- [x] CHK-032 [P0] The backfill spawns nothing from an untrusted checkout (T010). Evidence: `scratch/repro-after.txt` prints `fake CLI ran: false, fake hook ran: false`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n## Documentation\n\n- [x] CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `acceptance-criteria.md` state the same names, floors and fixed outputs. Evidence: `spec.md` REQ-001 now names `make no changes` and `no changes yet`, as T042 built them.\n- [x] CHK-041 [P1] The README, playbook, catalog, workflow and router edits match the code (T008, T017 to T024, T030 to T033): each verify prints what it says on the final tree. Evidence: the close-out `rg` reruns of T008, T017 to T021, T024 and T030 print what their lines name, `PBV` prints its `PASS` line, `DALL` reads `fail 0` and `scratch/repro-after.txt` prints the T031 to T033 probe lines.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n## File Organization\n\n- [x] CHK-050 [P1] The before and after records and the reproductions live in `scratch/` only, and no temporary probe or test folder remains. Evidence: the records are in `scratch/` only, and the `advisor-status` suite now removes every temporary tree it makes: a run of that file left the count of `advisor-status-*` folders in the system temp folder unchanged.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## Verification Summary\n\n| Category | Total | Verified |\n|----------|-------|----------|\n| P0 Items | 15 | 15/15 |\n| P1 Items | 8 | 8/8 |\n| P2 Items | 0 | 0/0 |\n\n**Verification Date**: 2026-11-13\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"sed -n '120,320p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/tasks.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794593454718,"end":1794593455097}}}}
