hing was scored: bad flags, a missing or malformed run log (`run_log_missing`, `run_log_malformed`), or a reader refusal printed with its own code such as `capability_gated` or `locator_unavailable`. |\n+| `command-offer.mjs` | Recovers the attribution fields for a run line. `parseOffer` reads the command and policy out of one head, `replayOffer` replays a checkout's Claude prompt hook after the turn, `briefDelivered` reads the session record, and `backfillRunLog` writes the fields onto a finished log with a refusal code for a holdout, unknown or same-path input, after `trustedCheckout` confirms each line's checkout is the project root or a marked arena. |\n+| `run-command-behaviour.mjs` | Runs one live turn per row and records the locator, exit and changed paths. `--print-argv <runtime>` prints a runtime's argv, `--list <set>` prints a set's row ids, and a run takes `--runtime` with `--set` or repeated `--row-id`, `--out <run-log>`, optional `--arm`, `--fixture` and `--dry-run`. Without `--arm`, a selection whose ids are all started-command rows runs under arm `g2`, one that holds none runs under `pre` and a mix is refused with `mixed_row_arms`. Each `g2` run line records the `fixture` folder its prompt named, and `--backfill` replays that folder, or `g2-fixture` beside the log for a line that holds none. `--backfill <run-log> --out <new-log> [--brief-only]` rewrites a finished log with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy` and `briefDelivered` instead of running a turn, and prints a JSON refusal with `same_path`, `holdout_row` or `unknown_row` when it cannot. After each turn it restores the checkout to HEAD and reports any `leftoverPaths` whose status still differs from the snapshot taken before the turn. Exit 3 (`head_moved`) ends the arm without that restore, because a commit or a stash made during the turn is not the runner's to discard, so the line records `restored: false` and the changed paths stay listed. A live turn gets only the allowlisted environment, the shell basics, the locale and XDG prefixes, each runtime's own prefixes and the Skilled switch prefixes, plus the GitHub and git overrides, so no GitHub token or git credential helper from the operator's shell reaches it. Exit 2 refuses instead of running: bad flags, an unknown runtime or set, a holdout or unknown row, a set with fewer rows than it needs (`set_short`), a dirty worktree outside the run log's folder (`worktree_dirty`), a checkout with a git remote (`remote_present`), a checkout without the arena builder's marker (`arena_unprepared`), a selection that mixes started-command rows with others (`mixed_row_arms`), or a Codex arm whose project hook is unapproved (`codex-hooks-unapproved`). |\n | `command-routing-baseline.json` | Captured command routing numbers that `tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` holds the scorer to. |\n | `build-holdout.mjs` | Builds the frozen holdout from three separately authored fixtures that are disjoint from the labeled corpus, copying each row's own label and keeping its provenance in `source_type` and `origin_fixture`. Family-normalized dedup keeps the first occurrence and drops any prompt that collides with the training corpus. `--write` rewrites `holdout-prompts.jsonl`. |\n | `capture-local-native-divergence-ledger.mjs` | Recomputes the strict Python/native top-1 divergence set the ratchet replays. An existing approval is kept only while its prompt hash and both current tops still match, so the output is a capture of live scoring rather than a hand-edited fixture. Scores both scorers against a skill graph indexed fresh into a temporary directory with the clock pinned to the capture day, and `--write` records the result. |\n@@ -123,7 +125,7 @@ A typed command travels on its owner. It is delivered only when the leading reco\n | `worktree-restore.mjs` | Restores one measured turn's checkout to the snapshot taken before it, leaving a path that was already dirty alone and dropping a staged path HEAD does not know. A second snapshot after the restore reports what still differs, so the caller fails the run instead of claiming a clean worktree. |\n | `ambiguity-prompts.jsonl` | Frozen ambiguity slice written by `derive-ambiguity-slice.mjs` and read by `capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs`. Each row carries `id`, `prompt`, `skill_top_1`, `bucket`, `source_type`, `tau`, `margin_at_capture` and `captured_at`. |\n | `doctor-prompts.jsonl` | Doctor routing slice read by `tests/doctor-routing-slice.vitest.ts`. Each row carries `id`, `prompt`, `expected_top`, `expected_second` and `wave`, where a wave scores only after every doctor bridge its rows expect is active, so a half-shipped bridge cannot fail the gate. |\n-| `holdout-prompts.jsonl` | Frozen holdout written by `build-holdout.mjs` from three separately authored fixtures disjoint from the labeled corpus, and read by `capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs` as its unseen split. |\n+| `holdout-prompts.jsonl` | Frozen holdout first written by `build-holdout.mjs` from three separately authored fixtures disjoint from the labeled corpus, and read by `capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs` as its unseen split. The file has been edited by hand since it was sealed, so `build-holdout.mjs --write` would now write a different set of rows. A sealed row is retired by deleting its line and recapturing `scorer-eval-baseline.json`, whose `holdoutSha256` fails the ratchet until that recapture runs. |\n | `labeled-prompts.jsonl` | Labeled training corpus with `id`, `prompt`, `skill_top_1`, `skill_correct`, `bucket`, `source_type`, `notes`, `gate3_triggers` and `gate3_reason_category`. Scored by `score-routing-corpus.py`, `score-outcome-rerank.mjs` and `capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs`, and read by the divergence ledger, the ambiguity deriver, the holdout builder and the gate 3 corpus runner. |\n | `scorer-eval-baseline.json` | Scorer eval baseline written by `capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs`: `schemaVersion`, `capturedAt`, `capturedAtSha`, `env`, the fixture hashes and `metrics` for the full corpus, holdout, ambiguity slice, gold-none false fire, intent buckets and unknown count. The ratchet gate re-scores live under the same environment and holds every metric to it. |\n \ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/scorer-eval-baseline.json b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/scorer-eval-baseline.json\nindex 7319bccba4..6b24ef192d 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/scorer-eval-baseline.json\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/scorer-eval-baseline.json\n@@ -1,9 +1,9 @@\n {\n   \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n   \"capturedAt\": \"2026-10-11\",\n-  \"capturedAtSha\": \"731967bc25\",\n+  \"capturedAtSha\": \"11f3a30814\",\n   \"corpusSha256\": \"sha256:4146b002802d010e4d9d3ddf4c07b0738e59a55fab590b2c51e1ed3d4da1e115\",\n-  \"holdoutSha256\": \"sha256:e8c637d3f59fbba18521c78bc238c5c86dc60d9f8b40c2c921c42ac49766a4cf\",\n+  \"holdoutSha256\": \"sha256:51cb48eb8b10e501fd8536eb403deb7674583f89adc5418c1cb583c5c6b02d6a\",\n   \"ambiguitySha256\": \"sha256:62423738cab74cf499d98f2e835e8e78c25e2b57e3c1b6994d8a2bd0bfb88491\",\n   \"env\": {\n     \"SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLE_BUILTIN_SEMANTIC\": \"1\",\n@@ -24,8 +24,8 @@\n     },\n     \"holdout_top1\": {\n       \"correct\": 50,\n-      \"total\": 66,\n-      \"accuracy\": 0.7576\n+      \"total\": 65,\n+      \"accuracy\": 0.7692\n     },\n     \"ambiguity_top1\": {\n       \"correct\": 21,\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/README.md b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/README.md\nindex f4fa050ad0..bfe7873606 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/README.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/README.md\n@@ -151,7 +151,7 @@ tests/\n | `routing-fixtures.affordance.test.ts` | Connects fixture prompts to affordance expectations. |\n | `shadow-sink.vitest.ts` | Covers shadow telemetry sink behavior. |\n | `skill-graph-db.vitest.ts` | Checks skill-graph database behavior used by advisor tests. |\n-| `manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts` | Verifies manual testing playbook routing fixtures. |\n+| `manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts` | Checks the playbook inventory: the root playbook lists every scenario file in the category tree once, and its persistence note names the folder results are recorded in. |\n | `skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts` | Verifies the stale-daemon retry in the CLI entrypoint. |\n | `prompt-policy-gold-replay.vitest.ts` | Replays the prompt gate over the labeled and golden corpora. |\n | `command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` | 17 cases on the meaning way in for a command row: a real cosine has to clear the bar and lead the other command rows by the margin, stand-in evidence never passes, a skill row is left alone, a meaning-passed command moves ahead of a passing skill only by the margin, and eligibility rules out every command on a no-edit request and all but read-only commands on a read-only question. |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff ec1869dae8..HEAD -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/scorer-eval-baseline.json .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/README.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794593519199,"end":1794593520102}}}}
