he `command` field is derived from the compiled route. The OpenCode plugin does not pass the option and keeps receiving `compiledRoute`. The option is declared in the zod schema (the `options` of `AdvisorRecommendInputSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`), the tool descriptor (`tools/advisor-recommend.ts:23`) and the CLI manifest (`skill-advisor-cli-manifest.ts:57`).\n \n-The request option `options.compiledRouteTopOnly` is an optional boolean that defaults to false. When a caller passes `true`, `enrichCompiledRoutes()` runs the route lookup for the first recommendation only and returns every later one unchanged, so only the top pick can carry `compiledRoute` or `command`. Each lookup is a `compiled-route.cjs` subprocess, so this saves one subprocess for each further eligible hub. The prompt hooks pass `true` with `includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the brief leads with the top pick. The option is declared in the zod schema (`schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:290`), the tool descriptor (`tools/advisor-recommend.ts:24`) and the CLI manifest (`skill-advisor-cli-manifest.ts:58`).\n+The request option `options.compiledRouteTopOnly` is an optional boolean that defaults to false. When a caller passes `true`, `enrichCompiledRoutes()` runs the route lookup for the first recommendation only and returns every later one unchanged, so only the top pick can carry `compiledRoute` or `command`. Each lookup is a `compiled-route.cjs` subprocess, so this saves one subprocess for each further eligible hub. The prompt hooks pass `true` with `includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the brief leads with the top pick. The option is declared in the zod schema (the `options` of `AdvisorRecommendInputSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`), the tool descriptor (`tools/advisor-recommend.ts:24`) and the CLI manifest (`skill-advisor-cli-manifest.ts:58`).\n \n A hub also leaves `command` off when the same command already ranks in the result through its own command row. `enrichCompiledRoutes()` takes the `command` fields present in the result as the commands already offered, so one command never takes two slots.\n \ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md\nindex ccf215f367..a4e6238b22 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\n ---\n title: \"Skill Advisor: Manual Testing Playbook\"\n description: \"Canonical sk-doc manual testing playbook for the Skill Advisor manual scenario corpus across the native command surface, runtime hooks, compatibility, daemon state, indexing, lifecycle, scorer and Python compatibility workflows.\"\n-version: 0.8.10.0\n+version: 0.8.11.0\n ---\n \n # Skill Advisor: Manual Testing Playbook\n@@ -27,7 +27,7 @@ Canonical package artifacts:\n ### Result persistence\n \n <!-- MANUAL_PLAYBOOK_RESULT_PERSISTENCE_CONTRACT -->\n-A scenario run is complete only after its `PASS`, `FAIL`, or `SKIP` outcome and reason are recorded into `system-skill-advisor/benchmark/reports/<dated-run-label>/`. Generated report Markdown is renderer-owned and never hand-authored.\n+A scenario run is complete only after its `PASS`, `FAIL` or `SKIP` outcome, its reason and its evidence paths are recorded by hand in `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/benchmark/reports/<dated-run-label>/`. The first recorded run creates that folder, because the wrapper that once wrote these records was retired and no renderer writes them now.\n \n ---\n \n@@ -37,7 +37,7 @@ This playbook provides 50 scenario files across 9 categories, one of them a live\n \n > **Numbering note (gap-09).** The directory layout skips slot `09--*` between `scorer-fusion` and `python-compat`. This mirrors the `feature-catalog/` 05-gap pattern and is an intentional historical reservation from initial scaffold design. The gap is preserved to keep spec-folder cross-reference stability across packets. Do not renumber.\n \n-Coverage note (2026-05-07): the prior operator scenario corpus now lives under `manual-testing-playbook/` as the canonical manual validation package. Former `SAD-NNN` IDs are deprecated plus mapped to current feature files in section 18. The source root index describes 42 scenarios, but the source category tree contains 41 `NNN-*.md` scenario files plus no `CL-002`. This root playbook reflects the live file inventory.\n+Coverage note (2026-05-07): the prior operator scenario corpus now lives under `manual-testing-playbook/` as the canonical manual validation package. Former `SAD-NNN` IDs are deprecated plus mapped to current feature files in section 18. The source root index describes 42 scenarios. The category tree holds 50 scenario files named by feature, none of them `NNN-*.md`, and still no `CL-002`. This root playbook reflects the live file inventory.\n \n ### Realistic Test Model\n \ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts\nindex d7410a6569..c9a906693b 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts\n@@ -53,6 +53,11 @@ describe('skill advisor manual testing playbook inventory', () => {\n     expect(rows).toHaveLength(50);\n     expect(new Set(rows.map((row) => row.id)).size).toBe(50);\n     expect(files).toHaveLength(50);\n+    expect(files.filter((file) => /\\/\\d{3}-[^/]*\\.md$/.test(file))).toHaveLength(0);\n+    expect(markdown).toContain(\n+      'The category tree holds 50 scenario files named by feature, none of them',\n+    );\n+    expect(markdown).not.toContain('scenario files plus no');\n \n     for (const row of rows) {\n       expect(existsSync(resolve(playbookRoot, row.relativePath))).toBe(true);\n@@ -60,4 +65,13 @@ describe('skill advisor manual testing playbook inventory', () => {\n \n     expect(rows.map((row) => row.relativePath).sort()).toEqual(files);\n   });\n+\n+  it('names the folder scenario results are recorded in by hand', () => {\n+    const markdown = readFileSync(rootPlaybook, 'utf8');\n+\n+    expect(markdown).toContain('<!-- MANUAL_PLAYBOOK_RESULT_PERSISTENCE_CONTRACT -->');\n+    expect(markdown).toContain('recorded by hand in');\n+    expect(markdown).toContain('system-skill-advisor/benchmark/reports/<dated-run-label>/');\n+    expect(markdown).not.toContain('renderer-owned');\n+  });\n });\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff ec1869dae8..HEAD -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794593550996,"end":1794593552476}}}}
