{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794593856305,"sessionID":"ses_e29e5c0b9ffed1u4GCgcaPeWZq","part":{"partID":"prt_1d62116b8002ko5s045vQxUVM4","sessionID":"ses_e29e5c0b9ffed1u4GCgcaPeWZq","messageID":"msg_1d61ff11a001zVHFV18h04mjmv","type":"tool","id":"call_490532562d4a4ddfbaca21ce","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"sed -n '660,760p' .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs"},"output":"function copyVerdict(expected, context, manifest, tools) {\n  if (expected.report_only) {\n    return { state: INFO, kind: 'reported only', detail: 'outside the checklist this command rewrites' };\n  }\n  if (expected.path.startsWith('~')) {\n    return { state: INFO, kind: 'outside the repository', detail: 'reported, never read' };\n  }\n\n  const target = path.join(context.root, expected.path);\n  if (expected.path.endsWith('.md') && expected.expect.includes('gate1-block-in-sync')) {\n    if (typeof tools.pointerSync !== 'string' || !fs.existsSync(tools.pointerSync)) {\n      return { state: UNKNOWN, kind: 'gate1 block unmeasured', detail: `the pointer sync is not installed at ${tools.pointerSync || '(no path)'}` };\n    }\n    const run = spawnSync(process.execPath, [tools.pointerSync, '--check', '--root', context.root], {\n      encoding: 'utf8',\n      timeout: TOOL_TIMEOUT_MS,\n    });\n    const output = `${run.stdout || ''}\\n${run.stderr || ''}`.split('\\n').map((line) => line.trim()).filter((line) => line !== '');\n    if (run.status === 0) return { state: PASS, kind: 'gate1 block in sync', detail: 'the generator reports no drift' };\n    if (run.status === 1) return { state: FINDING, kind: 'gate1 block out of sync', detail: output.join('; ') };\n    return { state: UNKNOWN, kind: 'gate1 block unmeasured', detail: output.join('; ') || `the pointer sync exited ${run.status}` };\n  }\n\n  const exists = fs.existsSync(target) || isSymlink(target);\n  const expectsAbsent = expected.expect.length === 1 && expected.expect[0] === 'absent';\n\n  if (expected.path === '.cursor/rules/repo-local.md') {\n    if (context.blockContent) {\n      if (!exists) return { state: FINDING, kind: 'mirror missing', detail: 'the block carries content and nothing mirrors it' };\n      const mirror = fs.readFileSync(target, 'utf8');\n      const missing = [...trimmedLines(context.block.content)].filter((line) => !mirror.includes(line));\n      return missing.length === 0\n        ? { state: PASS, kind: 'mirror current', detail: 'the mirror carries the block' }\n        : { state: FINDING, kind: 'mirror behind', detail: `${missing.length} block line(s) are not in the mirror` };\n    }\n    return exists\n      ? { state: FINDING, kind: 'mirror of an empty block', detail: 'the block is empty and a mirror exists' }\n      : { state: PASS, kind: 'absent', detail: 'no block content to mirror' };\n  }\n\n  // Claude Code reaches the root document only through this file, so its absence is a route\n  // the runtime does not have rather than a copy that is wrong.\n  if (expected.path === 'CLAUDE.md' && !exists && context.exists) {\n    return {\n      state: INFO,\n      kind: 'pointer missing',\n      detail: 'Claude Code reads only CLAUDE.md, so without a one-line @' + manifest.root_file + ' pointer it never loads ' + manifest.root_file,\n    };\n  }\n\n  if (!exists) {\n    return expectsAbsent\n      ? { state: PASS, kind: 'absent', detail: 'nothing to load twice' }\n      : { state: PASS, kind: 'absent', detail: 'absent, which the checklist allows' };\n  }\n\n  if (isSymlink(target)) {\n    const link = fs.readlinkSync(target);\n    // A path the checklist expects to be absent is one no runtime should load, and a link\n    // there loads the root document under that name just as a copy would.\n    if (expectsAbsent) {\n      return { state: FINDING, kind: 'symlink where none belongs', detail: `links to ${link}, where the checklist expects no file` };\n    }\n    const pointsAtRoot = path.basename(link) === manifest.root_file;\n    if (pointsAtRoot) return { state: PASS, kind: 'symlink', detail: `links to ${link}` };\n    return { state: FINDING, kind: 'symlink elsewhere', detail: `links to ${link} instead of ${manifest.root_file}` };\n  }\n\n  const content = fs.readFileSync(target, 'utf8');\n  if (!context.exists) {\n    return { state: FINDING, kind: 'sole instruction file', detail: `there is no ${manifest.root_file} for it to point at` };\n  }\n  if (content === context.text) {\n    return { state: FINDING, kind: 'identical copy', detail: `byte-identical to ${manifest.root_file}, so the two will drift` };\n  }\n\n  const unique = localLinesOf(content, context.text);\n  const rootLines = trimmedLines(context.text);\n  const sharesShippedLine = [...trimmedLines(content)].some((line) => rootLines.has(line));\n  const namesRoot = [...trimmedLines(content)].some((line) => line.includes(manifest.root_file));\n  // A pointer is a file that carries no shipped line and names the root document. Anything\n  // else is either a copy or a copy plus local lines, and both drift: the second also\n  // loses text when it is replaced, so the lines only it carries are listed.\n  if (!sharesShippedLine && namesRoot) {\n    return { state: PASS, kind: 'pointer', detail: `names ${manifest.root_file} and carries no shipped line` };\n  }\n  return { state: FINDING, kind: 'divergent copy', detail: `${unique.length} line(s) only this file carries`, lines: unique };\n}\n\nfunction isSymlink(target) {\n  try {\n    return fs.lstatSync(target).isSymbolicLink();\n  } catch {\n    return false;\n  }\n}\n\n// A11. The router: present, carrying the rows the template ships, and passing its own\n// checker. The checker's summary line is carried through, never rebuilt.\nfunction rowRouter(context, manifest, tools) {\n  const routerPath = path.join(context.root, manifest.router_file);\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"function copyVerdict(expected, context, manifest, tools) {\n  if (expected.report_only) {\n    return { state: INFO, kind: 'reported only', detail: 'outside the checklist this command rewrites' };\n  }\n  if (expected.path.startsWith('~')) {\n    return { state: INFO, kind: 'outside the repository', detail: 'reported, never read' };\n  }\n\n  const target = path.join(context.root, expected.path);\n  if (expected.path.endsWith('.md') && expected.expect.includes('gate1-block-in-sync')) {\n    if (typeof tools.pointerSync !== 'string' || !fs.existsSync(tools.pointerSync)) {\n      return { state: UNKNOWN, kind: 'gate1 block unmeasured', detail: `the pointer sync is not installed at ${tools.pointerSync || '(no path)'}` };\n    }\n    const run = spawnSync(process.execPath, [tools.pointerSync, '--check', '--root', context.root], {\n      encoding: 'utf8',\n      timeout: TOOL_TIMEOUT_MS,\n    });\n    const output = `${run.stdout || ''}\\n${run.stderr || ''}`.split('\\n').map((line) => line.trim()).filter((line) => line !== '');\n    if (run.status === 0) return { state: PASS, kind: 'gate1 block in sync', detail: 'the generator reports no drift' };\n    if (run.status === 1) return { state: FINDING, kind: 'gate1 block out of sync', detail: output.join('; ') };\n    return { state: UNKNOWN, kind: 'gate1 block unmeasured', detail: output.join('; ') || `the pointer sync exited ${run.status}` };\n  }\n\n  const exists = fs.existsSync(target) || isSymlink(target);\n  const expectsAbsent = expected.expect.length === 1 && expected.expect[0] === 'absent';\n\n  if (expected.path === '.cursor/rules/repo-local.md') {\n    if (context.blockContent) {\n      if (!exists) return { state: FINDING, kind: 'mirror missing', detail: 'the block carries content and nothing mirrors it' };\n      const mirror = fs.readFileSync(target, 'utf8');\n      const missing = [...trimmedLines(context.block.content)].filter((line) => !mirror.includes(line));\n      return missing.length === 0\n        ? { state: PASS, kind: 'mirror current', detail: 'the mirror carries the block' }\n        : { state: FINDING, kind: 'mirror behind', detail: `${missing.length} block line(s) are not in the mirror` };\n    }\n    return exists\n      ? { state: FINDING, kind: 'mirror of an empty block', detail: 'the block is empty and a mirror exists' }\n      : { state: PASS, kind: 'absent', detail: 'no block content to mirror' };\n  }\n\n  // Claude Code reaches the root document only through this file, so its absence is a route\n  // the runtime does not have rather than a copy that is wrong.\n  if (expected.path === 'CLAUDE.md' && !exists && context.exists) {\n    return {\n      state: INFO,\n      kind: 'pointer missing',\n      detail: 'Claude Code reads only CLAUDE.md, so without a one-line @' + manifest.root_file + ' pointer it never loads ' + manifest.root_file,\n    };\n  }\n\n  if (!exists) {\n    return expectsAbsent\n      ? { state: PASS, kind: 'absent', detail: 'nothing to load twice' }\n      : { state: PASS, kind: 'absent', detail: 'absent, which the checklist allows' };\n  }\n\n  if (isSymlink(target)) {\n    const link = fs.readlinkSync(target);\n    // A path the checklist expects to be absent is one no runtime should load, and a link\n    // there loads the root document under that name just as a copy would.\n    if (expectsAbsent) {\n      return { state: FINDING, kind: 'symlink where none belongs', detail: `links to ${link}, where the checklist expects no file` };\n    }\n    const pointsAtRoot = path.basename(link) === manifest.root_file;\n    if (pointsAtRoot) return { state: PASS, kind: 'symlink', detail: `links to ${link}` };\n    return { state: FINDING, kind: 'symlink elsewhere', detail: `links to ${link} instead of ${manifest.root_file}` };\n  }\n\n  const content = fs.readFileSync(target, 'utf8');\n  if (!context.exists) {\n    return { state: FINDING, kind: 'sole instruction file', detail: `there is no ${manifest.root_file} for it to point at` };\n  }\n  if (content === context.text) {\n    return { state: FINDING, kind: 'identical copy', detail: `byte-identical to ${manifest.root_file}, so the two will drift` };\n  }\n\n  const unique = localLinesOf(content, context.text);\n  const rootLines = trimmedLines(context.text);\n  const sharesShippedLine = [...trimmedLines(content)].some((line) => rootLines.has(line));\n  const namesRoot = [...trimmedLines(content)].some((line) => line.includes(manifest.root_file));\n  // A pointer is a file that carries no shipped line and names the root document. Anything\n  // else is either a copy or a copy plus local lines, and both drift: the second also\n  // loses text when it is replaced, so the lines only it carries are listed.\n  if (!sharesShippedLine && namesRoot) {\n    return { state: PASS, kind: 'pointer', detail: `names ${manifest.root_file} and carries no shipped line` };\n  }\n  return { state: FINDING, kind: 'divergent copy', detail: `${unique.length} line(s) only this file carries`, lines: unique };\n}\n\nfunction isSymlink(target) {\n  try {\n    return fs.lstatSync(target).isSymbolicLink();\n  } catch {\n    return false;\n  }\n}\n\n// A11. The router: present, carrying the rows the template ships, and passing its own\n// checker. The checker's summary line is carried through, never rebuilt.\nfunction rowRouter(context, manifest, tools) {\n  const routerPath = path.join(context.root, manifest.router_file);\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"sed -n '660,760p' .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs\"}"},"time":{"start":1794593855160,"end":1794593856305}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794593856328,"sessionID":"ses_e29e5c0b9ffed1u4GCgcaPeWZq","part":{"partID":"prt_1d62117cf001nwA4maFw5SGWSj","sessionID":"ses_e29e5c0b9ffed1u4GCgcaPeWZq","messageID":"msg_1d61ff11a001zVHFV18h04mjmv","type":"tool","id":"call_1040727a38324c0a90a2a2c0","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n \"function planDigest\" -A18 .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs | head -30; echo ===SCORER===; rg -n \"row-id narrows|rowId !== null|selectMode\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs | head -12"},"output":"466:function planDigest(composition, plan) {\n467-  const written = composition.files\n468-    .filter((file) => file.action === 'create' || file.action === 'replace')\n469-    .map((file) => [file.path, file.action, sha256(file.content)])\n470-    .sort((left, right) => (left[0] < right[0] ? -1 : left[0] > right[0] ? 1 : 0));\n471-  const removed = composition.files\n472-    .filter((file) => file.action === 'remove')\n473-    .map((file) => [file.path, file.action, null])\n474-    .sort((left, right) => (left[0] < right[0] ? -1 : left[0] > right[0] ? 1 : 0));\n475-  return sha256(JSON.stringify([composition.root, plan.base, plan.ordinal, ...written, ...removed]));\n476-}\n477-\n478-// Where each line of the old document sat, so a lost line is reported with the part it\n479-// belonged to. The block wins over the section it interrupts, because those bytes are the\n480-// repository's and not the section's.\n481-function placementOf(before) {\n482-  const places = new Map();\n483-  for (const section of before.sections) {\n484-    const place = section.id === null\n===SCORER===\n114:function selectMode(options) {\n123:  if (options.rowId !== null) throw new UsageError('--row-id narrows --summary only');\n1440:    mode = selectMode(options);\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"466:function planDigest(composition, plan) {\n467-  const written = composition.files\n468-    .filter((file) => file.action === 'create' || file.action === 'replace')\n469-    .map((file) => [file.path, file.action, sha256(file.content)])\n470-    .sort((left, right) => (left[0] < right[0] ? -1 : left[0] > right[0] ? 1 : 0));\n471-  const removed = composition.files\n472-    .filter((file) => file.action === 'remove')\n473-    .map((file) => [file.path, file.action, null])\n474-    .sort((left, right) => (left[0] < right[0] ? -1 : left[0] > right[0] ? 1 : 0));\n475-  return sha256(JSON.stringify([composition.root, plan.base, plan.ordinal, ...written, ...removed]));\n476-}\n477-\n478-// Where each line of the old document sat, so a lost line is reported with the part it\n479-// belonged to. The block wins over the section it interrupts, because those bytes are the\n480-// repository's and not the section's.\n481-function placementOf(before) {\n482-  const places = new Map();\n483-  for (const section of before.sections) {\n484-    const place = section.id === null\n===SCORER===\n114:function selectMode(options) {\n123:  if (options.rowId !== null) throw new UsageError('--row-id narrows --summary only');\n1440:    mode = selectMode(options);\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"rg -n \\\"function planDigest\\\" -A18 .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs | head -30; echo ===SCORER===; rg -n \\\"row-id narrows|rowId !== null|selectMode\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs | head -12\"}"},"time":{"start":1794593855439,"end":1794593856328}}}}
