scaffold files and renamed resources, or an in-place SKILL.md rewrite beside a new sibling ROUTER.md and the approved edge in its own graph-metadata.json), its backups under .skilled/skills/.state/doctor-sk-skill/<name>/<timestamp>/, the one scratch root the plain-skill path uses beside them at .skilled/skills/.state/doctor-sk-skill/<name>/scratch/ and deletes, the skill's changelog folder with its .skilled/changelog/<name> link, and the integration targets the plan records: the advisor graph .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/database/skill-graph.sqlite, the compiled skill-graph.json and the advisor cases file\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml:546:    gate3_location: \"AGENTS.md (created when absent, replaced with the shipped sections plus the composed block), CLAUDE.md and .codex/AGENTS.md (folded into the block and removed, unless --keep-claude-md), .cursor/rules/repo-local.md (the generated mirror of a non-empty block) and REPO RULES.md (missing shipped rows appended, or the file created behind --create-router), with a copy of every touched path taken to the plan's backup folder, .skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<first 16 characters of the plan digest>/ or the folder of that name under the operating system's temporary directory when git does not ignore that path, before the first byte, and .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md rewritten by the pointer generator the engine calls; the write runs only against the plan digest the operator approved\"\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"75:const BACKUP_DIR = path.join('.skilled', 'output', 'doctor-agents-md');\n76:const BACKUP_FALLBACK_DIR = 'doctor-agents-md';\n968:  const candidate = path.join(root, BACKUP_DIR);\n980:    ? `git does not ignore ${BACKUP_DIR} under ${root}`\n981:    : `git cannot answer whether ${BACKUP_DIR} is ignored under ${root} (exit ${ignored.status})`;\n===LINES===\n.skilled/commands/doctor/asset