uter), with a copy of every touched path taken to the plan's backup folder, .skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<first 16 characters of the plan digest>/ or the folder of that name under the operating system's temporary directory when git does not ignore that path, before the first byte, and .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md rewritten by the pointer generator the engine calls; the write runs only against the plan digest the operator approved\"\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"rg -n \\\"BACKUP_DIR|BACKUP_FALLBACK_DIR\\\" .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs | head -5; echo ===LINES===; rg -n \\\"first 16 characters|temporary directory|<timestamp>\\\" .skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml | head -10\"}"},"time":{"start":1794594225893,"end":1794594226761}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794594226771,"sessionID":"ses_e29e5c0b9ffed1u4GCgcaPeWZq","part":{"partID":"prt_1d626bb8a001tVzvBJ1N3fbmS0","sessionID":"ses_e29e5c0b9ffed1u4GCgcaPeWZq","messageID":"msg_1d6267702001S7uvOiCxkmCgbl","type":"tool","id":"call_8e85d31ba20448c4bdfdad7b","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n \"SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG\" .skilled/commands/doctor .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook | head -20; echo ===HOOKHEALTH===; rg -n \"hook health\" .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml | head -10"},"output":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/hooks-and-plugin/claude-hook.md:42:Each record carries `runtime`, taken from `SPECKIT_RUNTIME` when it names a known runtime and `claude` otherwise. Records carry optional `emittedBytes` and `directivesSuppressed`. The hook writes a health record to the diagnostics sink on every prompt and adds the skill label and the error text there only when `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` is set. A record whose answer came from the CLI's local scorer carries `degraded: true`. Raw prompts never appear in diagnostics. Before exiting, the hook waits up to 100 ms for pending diagnostic writes.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/compat-and-disable/global-disable-flag.md:81:4. One hook adapter. The spec-kit shim never forwards its child's stderr, so read the skipped record from the diagnostics JSONL that `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1` turns on:\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/compat-and-disable/global-disable-flag.md:87:  | SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED=1 SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1 node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/claude-user-prompt-submit.md:50:2. Run the hook through the shipped spec-kit shim with `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1`, and count the diagnostics JSONL lines before and after the call. The shim runs the advisor hook as a child process and never forwards that child's stderr, so the diagnostic record is read from the JSONL file the advisor hook appends to when `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` is set:\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/claude-user-prompt-submit.md:57:  | SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1 node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js \\\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/claude-user-prompt-submit.md:82:| SAD-003 | Claude hook additional context | Confirm prompt-time hook surfaces advisor context and fails open safely | `Role: Runtime hook operator. Context: current MCP server build and Claude UserPromptSubmit hook script. Action: pipe a realistic prompt payload into the hook, capture stdout and stderr separately and inspect additional context plus diagnostics. Format: return PASS or FAIL with context presence, prompt-safety result and exit code.` | 1. `bash: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime run build` -> 2. `bash: mkdir -p /tmp/skill-advisor-playbook` -> 3. `bash:` resolve `DIAG` with `advisorHookDiagnosticsPath(process.cwd())` and record its line count, as in step 2 above -> 4. `bash: printf '%s' '{\"prompt\":\"help me commit my changes\",\"cwd\":\"'\"$PWD\"'\",\"hook_event_name\":\"UserPromptSubmit\"}' \\| SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1 node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js > /tmp/skill-advisor-playbook/cl-001.stdout.json 2> /tmp/skill-advisor-playbook/cl-001.shim-stderr.txt` -> 5. `bash: echo \"Exit: $?\"` -> 6. `bash: tail -n 1 \"$DIAG\"` -> 7. `bash:` pipe the same payload into `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js` and capture its stderr | Exit code 0. Stdout is valid JSON and contains `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext`. For a matching prompt it starts with `Advisor:` and a freshness word (`live` or `stale`). With no brief it starts with one of the three status lines: `Advisor: outage (`, `Advisor: no skill matched.` or `Advisor: prompt skipped.` `{}` means the shim failed, which is a FAIL. The shim's own stderr is empty. The diagnostics JSONL gains one line, and that record has `runtime: \"claude\"`, `emittedBytes` and `directivesSuppressed`. The inner hook's stderr carries the same record shape. The raw prompt literal is absent from both | Preconditions:<br>`SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED=UNSET`<br>`hook script exists`<br><br>Shim transcript, 2026-09-26, stdout abbreviated after the first directive label:<br>`Exit: 0`<br>`diagnostic lines: 228 -> 229`<br>`{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"UserPromptSubmit\",\"additionalContext\":\"Advisor: live; use sk-git 0.95/0.12 pass.\\nDirectives:\\n- Comment hygiene [HARD BLOCK]: ...\"}}`<br>`{\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-26T20:03:24.005Z\",\"runtime\":\"claude\",\"status\":\"ok\",\"freshness\":\"live\",\"durationMs\":1755,\"cacheHit\":false,\"skillLabel\":\"sk-git\",\"emittedBytes\":259,\"directivesSuppressed\":false}`<br>`0`<br><br>Shim stderr: 0 bytes.<br><br>Inner hook stderr:<br>`{\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-26T20:03:25.450Z\",\"runtime\":\"claude\",\"status\":\"ok\",\"freshness\":\"live\",\"durationMs\":1257,\"cacheHit\":true,\"skillLabel\":\"sk-git\",\"emittedBytes\":259,\"directivesSuppressed\":false}`<br>`0` | PASS - exit code was `0`; stdout was valid JSON with `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` starting `Advisor: live`; the diagnostics JSONL went from 228 to 229 lines and the new record had `runtime: \"claude\"`, `emittedBytes` and `directivesSuppressed`; the prompt literal `help me commit my changes` matched 0 times in the JSONL and in the inner hook's stderr. | 1. Verify compiled hook exists; 2. Rebuild MCP server; 3. Run `advisor_status`; 4. Confirm disable flag is unset; 5. Inspect hook parity tests |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/claude-user-prompt-submit.md:101:| No new diagnostics line | `AFTER` equals `BEFORE` | Confirm `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1` reached the shim call and that `DIAG` resolved from the repository root. |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-setup-contract.test.cjs:86:  assert.doesNotMatch(SETUP_ROUTER, /SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG/);\n===HOOKHEALTH===\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml:59:    - \"Leg advisor: run node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --format json --timeout-ms 500 --warm-only. Exit 0 with data.freshness set to live is PASS. Exit 0 with any other freshness is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor rebuild. Exit 75 with a staleDistWarning field in stderr JSON is FAIL, with repair npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build. Exit 75 without that field is SKIP because the daemon is not running. Any other exit is FAIL, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor rebuild. When data.hookHealth is present, show hook p95 <rollingP95Ms> ms over <invocations> prompts, fail-open <rollingFailOpenRate as a percent>, degraded <rollingDegradedRate as a percent> and last record <lastRecordAt> under the leg. It never changes the leg's status. When data.hookHealth is absent, show hook health not recorded under the leg, because no prompt hook has written a record for this checkout yet: OpenCode has no prompt hook that writes one and an unapproved Codex hook never runs. It never changes the leg's status.\"\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/hooks-and-plugin/claude-hook.md:42:Each record carries `runtime`, taken from `SPECKIT_RUNTIME` when it names a known runtime and `claude` otherwise. Records carry optional `emittedBytes` and `directivesSuppressed`. The hook writes a health record to the diagnostics sink on every prompt and adds the skill label and the error text there only when `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` is set. A record whose answer came from the CLI's local scorer carries `degraded: true`. Raw prompts never appear in diagnostics. Before exiting, the hook waits up to 100 ms for pending diagnostic writes.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/compat-and-disable/global-disable-flag.md:81:4. One hook adapter. The spec-kit shim never forwards its child's stderr, so read the skipped record from the diagnostics JSONL that `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1` turns on:\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/compat-and-disable/global-disable-flag.md:87:  | SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED=1 SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1 node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/claude-user-prompt-submit.md:50:2. Run the hook through the shipped spec-kit shim with `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1`, and count the diagnostics JSONL lines before and after the call. The shim runs the advisor hook as a child process and never forwards that child's stderr, so the diagnostic record is read from the JSONL file the advisor hook appends to when `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` is set:\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/claude-user-prompt-submit.md:57:  | SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1 node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js \\\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/claude-user-prompt-submit.md:82:| SAD-003 | Claude hook additional context | Confirm prompt-time hook surfaces advisor context and fails open safely | `Role: Runtime hook operator. Context: current MCP server build and Claude UserPromptSubmit hook script. Action: pipe a realistic prompt payload into the hook, capture stdout and stderr separately and inspect additional context plus diagnostics. Format: return PASS or FAIL with context presence, prompt-safety result and exit code.` | 1. `bash: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime run build` -> 2. `bash: mkdir -p /tmp/skill-advisor-playbook` -> 3. `bash:` resolve `DIAG` with `advisorHookDiagnosticsPath(process.cwd())` and record its line count, as in step 2 above -> 4. `bash: printf '%s' '{\"prompt\":\"help me commit my changes\",\"cwd\":\"'\"$PWD\"'\",\"hook_event_name\":\"UserPromptSubmit\"}' \\| SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1 node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js > /tmp/skill-advisor-playbook/cl-001.stdout.json 2> /tmp/skill-advisor-playbook/cl-001.shim-stderr.txt` -> 5. `bash: echo \"Exit: $?\"` -> 6. `bash: tail -n 1 \"$DIAG\"` -> 7. `bash:` pipe the same payload into `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js` and capture its stderr | Exit code 0. Stdout is valid JSON and contains `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext`. For a matching prompt it starts with `Advisor:` and a freshness word (`live` or `stale`). With no brief it starts with one of the three status lines: `Advisor: outage (`, `Advisor: no skill matched.` or `Advisor: prompt skipped.` `{}` means the shim failed, which is a FAIL. The shim's own stderr is empty. The diagnostics JSONL gains one line, and that record has `runtime: \"claude\"`, `emittedBytes` and `directivesSuppressed`. The inner hook's stderr carries the same record shape. The raw prompt literal is absent from both | Preconditions:<br>`SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED=UNSET`<br>`hook script exists`<br><br>Shim transcript, 2026-09-26, stdout abbreviated after the first directive label:<br>`Exit: 0`<br>`diagnostic lines: 228 -> 229`<br>`{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"UserPromptSubmit\",\"additionalContext\":\"Advisor: live; use sk-git 0.95/0.12 pass.\\nDirectives:\\n- Comment hygiene [HARD BLOCK]: ...\"}}`<br>`{\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-26T20:03:24.005Z\",\"runtime\":\"claude\",\"status\":\"ok\",\"freshness\":\"live\",\"durationMs\":1755,\"cacheHit\":false,\"skillLabel\":\"sk-git\",\"emittedBytes\":259,\"directivesSuppressed\":false}`<br>`0`<br><br>Shim stderr: 0 bytes.<br><br>Inner hook stderr:<br>`{\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-26T20:03:25.450Z\",\"runtime\":\"claude\",\"status\":\"ok\",\"freshness\":\"live\",\"durationMs\":1257,\"cacheHit\":true,\"skillLabel\":\"sk-git\",\"emittedBytes\":259,\"directivesSuppressed\":false}`<br>`0` | PASS - exit code was `0`; stdout was valid JSON with `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` starting `Advisor: live`; the diagnostics JSONL went from 228 to 229 lines and the new record had `runtime: \"claude\"`, `emittedBytes` and `directivesSuppressed`; the prompt literal `help me commit my changes` matched 0 times in the JSONL and in the inner hook's stderr. | 1. Verify compiled hook exists; 2. Rebuild MCP server; 3. Run `advisor_status`; 4. Confirm disable flag is unset; 5. Inspect hook parity tests |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/claude-user-prompt-submit.md:101:| No new diagnostics line | `AFTER` equals `BEFORE` | Confirm `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1` reached the shim call and that `DIAG` resolved from the repository root. |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-setup-contract.test.cjs:86:  assert.doesNotMatch(SETUP_ROUTER, /SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG/);\n===HOOKHEALTH===\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml:59:    - \"Leg advisor: run node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --format json --timeout-ms 500 --warm-only. Exit 0 with data.freshness set to live is PASS. Exit 0 with any other freshness is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor rebuild. Exit 75 with a staleDistWarning field in stderr JSON is FAIL, with repair npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build. Exit 75 without that field is SKIP because the daemon is not running. Any other exit is FAIL, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor rebuild. When data.hookHealth is present, show hook p95 <rollingP95Ms> ms over <invocations> prompts, fail-open <rollingFailOpenRate as a percent>, degraded <rollingDegradedRate as a percent> and last record <lastRecordAt> under the leg. It never changes the leg's status. When data.hookHealth is absent, show hook health not recorded under the leg, because no prompt hook has written a record for this checkout yet: OpenCode has no prompt hook that writes one and an unapproved Codex hook never runs. It never changes the leg's status.\"\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"rg -n \\\"SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG\\\" .skilled/commands/doctor .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook | head -20; echo ===HOOKHEALTH===; rg -n \\\"hook health\\\" .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml | head -10\"}"},"time":{"start":1794594225034,"end":1794594226771}}}}
