{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794594296816,"sessionID":"ses_e29e5c0b9ffed1u4GCgcaPeWZq","part":{"partID":"prt_1d627d012001nxkX99sGflqSDb","sessionID":"ses_e29e5c0b9ffed1u4GCgcaPeWZq","messageID":"msg_1d62797d90017LoA4B4a7TV34V","type":"tool","id":"call_336d3f34d32e421caa68c68f","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n \"50 scenario|no \\`CL-002\\`|42 scenarios\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md; find .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook -mindepth 2 -type f -name '*.md' | wc -l; echo ===BASE===; python3 -c \"print(round(50/65,4), round(50/66,4))\""},"output":"36:This playbook provides 50 scenario files across 9 categories, one of them a live conversation scenario, validating the Skill Advisor surface. Scenario IDs use a multi-prefix scheme: `NC` for the native command surface, `CL` for CLI hooks plus plugin behavior, `CP` for compatibility plus disable controls, `OP` for operator H5 states, `AU` for auto-update daemon behavior, `AI` for auto-indexing, `LC` for lifecycle routing, `SC` for scorer fusion and `PC` for Python compatibility.\n40:Coverage note (2026-05-07): the prior operator scenario corpus now lives under `manual-testing-playbook/` as the canonical manual validation package. Former `SAD-NNN` IDs are deprecated plus mapped to current feature files in section 18. The source root index describes 42 scenarios. The category tree holds 50 scenario files named by feature, none of them `NNN-*.md`, and still no `CL-002`. This root playbook reflects the live file inventory.\n133:Release is `READY` only when all 50 scenario files are `PASS` or have an approved `SKIP` with a real blocker and no prompt-safety, rebuild, daemon, indexing, lifecycle, scorer or compatibility failure remains unresolved.\n      50\n===BASE===\n0.7692 0.7576\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"36:This playbook provides 50 scenario files across 9 categories, one of them a live conversation scenario, validating the Skill Advisor surface. Scenario IDs use a multi-prefix scheme: `NC` for the native command surface, `CL` for CLI hooks plus plugin behavior, `CP` for compatibility plus disable controls, `OP` for operator H5 states, `AU` for auto-update daemon behavior, `AI` for auto-indexing, `LC` for lifecycle routing, `SC` for scorer fusion and `PC` for Python compatibility.\n40:Coverage note (2026-05-07): the prior operator scenario corpus now lives under `manual-testing-playbook/` as the canonical manual validation package. Former `SAD-NNN` IDs are deprecated plus mapped to current feature files in section 18. The source root index describes 42 scenarios. The category tree holds 50 scenario files named by feature, none of them `NNN-*.md`, and still no `CL-002`. This root playbook reflects the live file inventory.\n133:Release is `READY` only when all 50 scenario files are `PASS` or have an approved `SKIP` with a real blocker and no prompt-safety, rebuild, daemon, indexing, lifecycle, scorer or compatibility failure remains unresolved.\n      50\n===BASE===\n0.7692 0.7576\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"rg -n \\\"50 scenario|no \\\\`CL-002\\\\`|42 scenarios\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md; find .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook -mindepth 2 -type f -name '*.md' | wc -l; echo ===BASE===; python3 -c \\\"print(round(50/65,4), round(50/66,4))\\\"\"}"},"time":{"start":1794594295826,"end":1794594296816}}}}
