g-check.cjs\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml:61:    - \"Leg delivery: run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\" and node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\", and show each line they print under the leg. Both exit 0 is PASS. A hook-missing line is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors in a Skilled checkout or /doctor:symlink check in a linked project. WARN codex-hooks-unapproved is DEGRADED, with the repair line the check printed. WARN codex-advisor-hook-absent is DEGRADED, with the repair line the check printed. Exit 2 from either check is ERROR. This leg is never FAIL, because a hook that is not wired or not approved stops the brief, not the install.\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml:48:  check_engine: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml:74:      - \"Check that .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs, .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs, .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/lib/agents-md-sections.cjs and .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json exist. If any is missing, report the missing path and stop with STATUS=FAIL. An embed without its engine or its manifest would invent a template.\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml:110:      - \"Run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs once, with --root \\\"{root}\\\" when this run was pointed at another repository, and read the twelve rows against the plan's claims: the block the plan composed is the block on disk, and the paths the apply printed as written are the paths the check reads.\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml:525:    yaml: doctor-agents-md-check.yaml\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2026-11-13T18:26:00