{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794594411580,"sessionID":"ses_e29e5c0b9ffed1u4GCgcaPeWZq","part":{"partID":"prt_1d6298fdd001Dq1ylDzH7Aia5H","sessionID":"ses_e29e5c0b9ffed1u4GCgcaPeWZq","messageID":"msg_1d6296f9300192eJTh1VEx7QD8","type":"tool","id":"call_af4a003f43c34d9bbb28bd30","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n \"A10|runtime copies\" .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-check.yaml .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt 2>/dev/null | head -10"},"output":".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-check.yaml:5:purpose: Report rows A1 to A12 for the root AGENTS.md, its repo-local block, its runtime copies and its REPO RULES.md router, by running the shipped check engine once and naming the repair for each finding\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-check.yaml:55:    - \"The engine reads the target's root document, its runtime copies and its REPO RULES.md against the shipped manifest and reports twelve rows, each PASS, FINDING, UNKNOWN or INFO. An UNKNOWN row means the row could not be answered, never that it passed, and an INFO row reports a fact the row does not grade.\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-check.yaml:58:    - \"A10 reports each runtime copy the manifest expects, A11 the REPO RULES.md rows through the repo-rules checker, and A12 the template purity of the shipped body. The three rows the engine must not invent belong to the tools this workflow never re-implements: the canary, the pointer sync and the repo-rules checker.\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt:71:The twelve rows are A1 install state, A2 sections present, A3 order and numbering, A4 section currency, A5 pins, A6 delivery budget, A7 repo-local block, A8 unmarked repo-unique content, A9 unmarked local edits, A10 runtime copies, A11 REPO RULES.md and A12 template purity. Read A1 first: it says which state the repository is in, and every other row is a detail of that state. A8 and A9 are the two rows that name a line somebody wrote, so quote them in full.\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt:268:| `A10` reports a runtime copy out of sync, or the apply's `pointer-sync:` line reported a nonzero exit | The generator rewrites an existing `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` and never creates a missing one, so a missing file stays missing however often the embed reruns. `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` lists the generated runtime mirrors that drift, each with the write form of the checker that owns it; the pointer block is not one of the files that route checks, so a `missing` line on it means the file has to exist first. Create `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md`, run `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs --root <root>`, then rerun `/doctor:agents-md check` and read `A10` again |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt:284:| The apply's `pointer-sync:` line reported a nonzero exit | `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` | It lists each generated runtime mirror that drifts with the write form of its checker, and `A10` names the copy that is still unverified |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-check.yaml:5:purpose: Report rows A1 to A12 for the root AGENTS.md, its repo-local block, its runtime copies and its REPO RULES.md router, by running the shipped check engine once and naming the repair for each finding\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-check.yaml:55:    - \"The engine reads the target's root document, its runtime copies and its REPO RULES.md against the shipped manifest and reports twelve rows, each PASS, FINDING, UNKNOWN or INFO. An UNKNOWN row means the row could not be answered, never that it passed, and an INFO row reports a fact the row does not grade.\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-check.yaml:58:    - \"A10 reports each runtime copy the manifest expects, A11 the REPO RULES.md rows through the repo-rules checker, and A12 the template purity of the shipped body. The three rows the engine must not invent belong to the tools this workflow never re-implements: the canary, the pointer sync and the repo-rules checker.\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt:71:The twelve rows are A1 install state, A2 sections present, A3 order and numbering, A4 section currency, A5 pins, A6 delivery budget, A7 repo-local block, A8 unmarked repo-unique content, A9 unmarked local edits, A10 runtime copies, A11 REPO RULES.md and A12 template purity. Read A1 first: it says which state the repository is in, and every other row is a detail of that state. A8 and A9 are the two rows that name a line somebody wrote, so quote them in full.\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt:268:| `A10` reports a runtime copy out of sync, or the apply's `pointer-sync:` line reported a nonzero exit | The generator rewrites an existing `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` and never creates a missing one, so a missing file stays missing however often the embed reruns. `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` lists the generated runtime mirrors that drift, each with the write form of the checker that owns it; the pointer block is not one of the files that route checks, so a `missing` line on it means the file has to exist first. Create `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md`, run `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs --root <root>`, then rerun `/doctor:agents-md check` and read `A10` again |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt:284:| The apply's `pointer-sync:` line reported a nonzero exit | `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` | It lists each generated runtime mirror that drifts with the write form of its checker, and `A10` names the copy that is still unverified |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"rg -n \\\"A10|runtime copies\\\" .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-check.yaml .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt 2>/dev/null | head -10\"}"},"time":{"start":1794594410461,"end":1794594411580}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794594411591,"sessionID":"ses_e29e5c0b9ffed1u4GCgcaPeWZq","part":{"partID":"prt_1d6298bb1001LMfuSTuldVHGDt","sessionID":"ses_e29e5c0b9ffed1u4GCgcaPeWZq","messageID":"msg_1d6296f9300192eJTh1VEx7QD8","type":"tool","id":"call_1e4c59cdda59426dadd43fd0","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n \"hook-wiring-check\" .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml | head; echo ===EXPORTS===; rg -n \"module.exports\" .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs; echo ===SHELL===; rg -n \"spawnSync|execSync|exec\\(\" .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs"},"output":".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml:40:  hook_wiring_check: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml:61:    - \"Leg delivery: run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\" and node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\", and show each line they print under the leg. Both exit 0 is PASS. A hook-missing line is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors in a Skilled checkout or /doctor:symlink check in a linked project. WARN codex-hooks-unapproved is DEGRADED, with the repair line the check printed. WARN codex-advisor-hook-absent is DEGRADED, with the repair line the check printed. Exit 2 from either check is ERROR. This leg is never FAIL, because a hook that is not wired or not approved stops the brief, not the install.\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml:37:  hook_wiring: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml:60:    - 'After the engine report, run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \"{root}\" to read the prompt hook entry each installed runtime loads. It skips a runtime whose folder is absent. Show every hook-missing <runtime> line as printed. Exit 0 leaves the status unchanged. Exit 1 ends the run with STATUS=WARN and names the repair: copy the prompt hook entry from the matching file in the Skilled checkout into the target file for that runtime. Exit 2 means the check was refused: quote its message and end with STATUS=FAIL.'\n===EXPORTS===\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:1070:module.exports = {\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:347:module.exports = { main, eventPayload };\n===SHELL===\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":1},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml:40:  hook_wiring_check: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml:61:    - \"Leg delivery: run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\" and node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\", and show each line they print under the leg. Both exit 0 is PASS. A hook-missing line is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors in a Skilled checkout or /doctor:symlink check in a linked project. WARN codex-hooks-unapproved is DEGRADED, with the repair line the check printed. WARN codex-advisor-hook-absent is DEGRADED, with the repair line the check printed. Exit 2 from either check is ERROR. This leg is never FAIL, because a hook that is not wired or not approved stops the brief, not the install.\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml:37:  hook_wiring: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml:60:    - 'After the engine report, run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \"{root}\" to read the prompt hook entry each installed runtime loads. It skips a runtime whose folder is absent. Show every hook-missing <runtime> line as printed. Exit 0 leaves the status unchanged. Exit 1 ends the run with STATUS=WARN and names the repair: copy the prompt hook entry from the matching file in the Skilled checkout into the target file for that runtime. Exit 2 means the check was refused: quote its message and end with STATUS=FAIL.'\n===EXPORTS===\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:1070:module.exports = {\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:347:module.exports = { main, eventPayload };\n===SHELL===\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Exit code: 1"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"rg -n \\\"hook-wiring-check\\\" .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml | head; echo ===EXPORTS===; rg -n \\\"module.exports\\\" .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs; echo ===SHELL===; rg -n \\\"spawnSync|execSync|exec\\\\(\\\" .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\"}"},"time":{"start":1794594409393,"end":1794594411591}}}}
