{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794594432974,"sessionID":"ses_e29e5c0b9ffed1u4GCgcaPeWZq","part":{"partID":"prt_1d629b68b001pWR35wnn5J5x3m","sessionID":"ses_e29e5c0b9ffed1u4GCgcaPeWZq","messageID":"msg_1d62997e1001SqJZ6BXVZd7LDx","type":"tool","id":"call_0eac813383144cf68a5e3a88","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 004\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Lineage: `doctor-docs-3`, session `fanout-doctor-docs-3-1794593402980-zhrui5`, generation 1.\n- Mode: review, dimension `security`, budget profile `adjudicate`.\n- Operator review focus: pass-three narrow review of the doctor-docs files changed by the pass-two remediation commits, each change judged against its task line and its callers. This iteration addresses the focus by walking the callers of both changed check engines, re-reading the carried P1 against its counterevidence, and auditing the changed surfaces for execution, path or secret exposure.\n- Sources read: `doctor-setup.yaml:40,61`, `doctor-symlink-check.yaml:37,60`, `doctor-agents-md-check.yaml:34,54-58`, `doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml:48,74,110`, `doctor-agents-md-restore.yaml:42,62,95`, `doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt:71,268,284`, `hook-wiring-check.cjs:300-347`, `agents-md-check.cjs:1070-1080`, and the carried finding at `hook-wiring-check.cjs:264-269`.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:300-347` (caller surface: `main`, `inspect`, exports)\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:1040-1080` (export surface)\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml:40,61` (caller: delivery leg)\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml:37,60` (caller: symlink route)\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-check.yaml:34,54-58`\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml:48,74,110`\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-restore.yaml:42,62,95`\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone new. The carried finding `DR3-P1-001` stays active: re-reading `hook-wiring-check.cjs:264-269` confirms that `NODE_FLAGS_WITHOUT_RUN.has(flag)` tests the whole token, so `--eval=0`, `-e\"1\"` and `-p\"1\"` never match, and the marker is then accepted as node's script word. The counterevidence searched is unchanged: no later re-test of the marker as an argument, and no test covers the attached spelling. Final severity stays P1 because the check's stated contract is to read the command the way a shell runs it, and the caller at `doctor-setup.yaml:61` turns the false `ok claude` into a PASS delivery leg.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | pass | The caller surface matches the changed behavior: both doctor routes read the check's printed lines and its exit codes, and neither parses the internal flag tables. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | CHK-FIX-005's matrix covers the space-separated forms only, which is the exact gap the carried P1 names; no checklist row claims the attached form. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | pass | Closed in iteration 3. |\n| `playbook_capability` | pass | Closed in iteration 3. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `doctor-setup.yaml:61` maps exit 0 to PASS and a `hook-missing` line to DEGRADED, so the false `ok claude` has a named consumer and a user-visible status effect.\n- `doctor-symlink-check.yaml:60` maps exit 0 to an unchanged status and exit 1 to WARN, the second consumer of the same wrong result.\n- `hook-wiring-check.cjs` holds no `spawnSync`, `execSync` or `exec` call: it parses the settings JSON and never runs the command string, so the reader adds no execution surface.\n- `agents-md-check.cjs` exports `main` and its row helpers; the four doctor assets that call it read the printed rows and never parse the A10 detail's first number.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- A `--root` that names another checkout is still read-only: `inspect` joins the constant runtime file names onto the root and reads them, with no write path.\n- The temporary-directory backup fallback is printed by the embed engine and consumed by the restore route as a path, not evaluated; no shell interpolation reaches it.\n- The changed docs name no credentials, tokens or environment values that would expose a secret; `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` was removed from the setup router rather than added.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- No changed line in the doctor scripts executes, eval-loads or interpolates the shell command it reads.\n- The two check engines keep their exported surface (`main`, `eventPayload`), so every caller keeps working.\n- The A10 detail change has no machine parser outside its own test.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- A security finding on the reader is ruled out: it treats the settings file as data and never spawns a process.\n- A caller regression from the A10 detail change is ruled out: the doctor assets render rows and read states, and no asset reads the detail's leading count.\n- A path-traversal finding on `--root` is ruled out: the joined names are constants from the runtime table, and the check only reads them.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- None: all four dimensions are covered, the convergence ratio is 0 for the last three iterations and the only open finding is the carried P1. Synthesis follows.\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-3/iterations/iteration-004.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-3/iterations/iteration-004.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-3/iterations/iteration-004.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 004\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Lineage: `doctor-docs-3`, session `fanout-doctor-docs-3-1794593402980-zhrui5`, generation 1.\\n- Mode: review, dimension `security`, budget profile `adjudicate`.\\n- Operator review focus: pass-three narrow review of the doctor-docs files changed by the pass-two remediation commits, each change judged against its task line and its callers. This iteration addresses the focus by walking the callers of both changed check engines, re-reading the carried P1 against its counterevidence, and auditing the changed surfaces for execution, path or secret exposure.\\n- Sources read: `doctor-setup.yaml:40,61`, `doctor-symlink-check.yaml:37,60`, `doctor-agents-md-check.yaml:34,54-58`, `doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml:48,74,110`, `doctor-agents-md-restore.yaml:42,62,95`, `doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt:71,268,284`, `hook-wiring-check.cjs:300-347`, `agents-md-check.cjs:1070-1080`, and the carried finding at `hook-wiring-check.cjs:264-269`.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:300-347` (caller surface: `main`, `inspect`, exports)\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:1040-1080` (export surface)\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml:40,61` (caller: delivery leg)\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml:37,60` (caller: symlink route)\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-check.yaml:34,54-58`\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml:48,74,110`\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-restore.yaml:42,62,95`\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone new. The carried finding `DR3-P1-001` stays active: re-reading `hook-wiring-check.cjs:264-269` confirms that `NODE_FLAGS_WITHOUT_RUN.has(flag)` tests the whole token, so `--eval=0`, `-e\\\"1\\\"` and `-p\\\"1\\\"` never match, and the marker is then accepted as node's script word. The counterevidence searched is unchanged: no later re-test of the marker as an argument, and no test covers the attached spelling. Final severity stays P1 because the check's stated contract is to read the command the way a shell runs it, and the caller at `doctor-setup.yaml:61` turns the false `ok claude` into a PASS delivery leg.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | pass | The caller surface matches the changed behavior: both doctor routes read the check's printed lines and its exit codes, and neither parses the internal flag tables. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | CHK-FIX-005's matrix covers the space-separated forms only, which is the exact gap the carried P1 names; no checklist row claims the attached form. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | pass | Closed in iteration 3. |\\n| `playbook_capability` | pass | Closed in iteration 3. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `doctor-setup.yaml:61` maps exit 0 to PASS and a `hook-missing` line to DEGRADED, so the false `ok claude` has a named consumer and a user-visible status effect.\\n- `doctor-symlink-check.yaml:60` maps exit 0 to an unchanged status and exit 1 to WARN, the second consumer of the same wrong result.\\n- `hook-wiring-check.cjs` holds no `spawnSync`, `execSync` or `exec` call: it parses the settings JSON and never runs the command string, so the reader adds no execution surface.\\n- `agents-md-check.cjs` exports `main` and its row helpers; the four doctor assets that call it read the printed rows and never parse the A10 detail's first number.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- A `--root` that names another checkout is still read-only: `inspect` joins the constant runtime file names onto the root and reads them, with no write path.\\n- The temporary-directory backup fallback is printed by the embed engine and consumed by the restore route as a path, not evaluated; no shell interpolation reaches it.\\n- The changed docs name no credentials, tokens or environment values that would expose a secret; `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` was removed from the setup router rather than added.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- No changed line in the doctor scripts executes, eval-loads or interpolates the shell command it reads.\\n- The two check engines keep their exported surface (`main`, `eventPayload`), so every caller keeps working.\\n- The A10 detail change has no machine parser outside its own test.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- A security finding on the reader is ruled out: it treats the settings file as data and never spawns a process.\\n- A caller regression from the A10 detail change is ruled out: the doctor assets render rows and read states, and no asset reads the detail's leading count.\\n- A path-traversal finding on `--root` is ruled out: the joined names are constants from the runtime table, and the check only reads them.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- None: all four dimensions are covered, the convergence ratio is 0 for the last three iterations and the only open finding is the carried P1. Synthesis follows.\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-3/iterations/iteration-004.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794594420363,"end":1794594432974}}}}
