{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794594539708,"sessionID":"ses_e29e5c0b9ffed1u4GCgcaPeWZq","part":{"partID":"prt_1d62b251b001Y4zCkUFwl5eZpe","sessionID":"ses_e29e5c0b9ffed1u4GCgcaPeWZq","messageID":"msg_1d62b0103001Ju1Cj1ncqMNPrY","type":"tool","id":"call_18ff928b495f446a968b982e","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Deep Review Report: doctor-docs-3\n\nLineage `doctor-docs-3` of the command-surfacing pass-three fan-out. Session `fanout-doctor-docs-3-1794593402980-zhrui5`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`. Review target `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`, review target type spec-folder. Base commit `ec1869dae8`, head `1ca14a4498`.\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\n- Overall verdict: **CONDITIONAL**\n- hasAdvisories: false\n- Active findings: P0 = 0, P1 = 1, P2 = 0\n- Review scope: the 16 doctor-docs files changed by the two pass-two remediation commits, each read through `git diff ec1869dae8..HEAD`, plus the callers of their changed functions. Pass-one and pass-two findings whose fixes hold are excluded, as are the four coordinator-left items.\n- Operator review focus: Code review of command surfacing, PASS THREE (narrow). FIRST read the full instructions in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/c9fe91ef-9b85-4bdc-88fb-4d6f766eaecf/scratchpad/review-instructions-3.txt and follow them exactly. Scope file: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/c9fe91ef-9b85-4bdc-88fb-4d6f766eaecf/scratchpad/review-scope-3.txt (area TAB path). Review only the files whose area equals your lineage label without its -3 suffix, by reading git diff ec1869dae8..HEAD for each. Every finding is P0, P1 or P2 with file:line and a concrete input. Never open holdout-prompts.jsonl or read holdout prompt text. Change no code, write only inside your lineage folder.\n- Four iterations covered correctness, traceability, maintainability and security. The changed doctor contracts, READMEs, playbook, catalog and baseline are clean; the one defect is in the new node-flag reader in the doctor hook-wiring check.\n\n## 2. Planning Trigger\n\n`/speckit:plan` is required because one active P1 remains. Planning Packet:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"triggered\": true,\n  \"verdict\": \"CONDITIONAL\",\n  \"hasAdvisories\": false,\n  \"activeFindings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"DR3-P1-001\",\n      \"severity\": \"P1\",\n      \"title\": \"An attached node evaluation flag still reports the hook as wired\",\n      \"dimension\": \"correctness\",\n      \"file\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:266\",\n      \"evidence\": \"NODE_FLAGS_WITHOUT_RUN is tested with exact membership on the whole token, so --eval=0, -e\\\"1\\\" and -p\\\"1\\\" skip the guard; the marker then matches as node's script word\",\n      \"impact\": \"node hook-wiring-check.cjs --root . prints ok claude and exits 0 for a command that never runs the marker; doctor-setup.yaml:61 turns that into a PASS delivery leg and doctor-symlink-check.yaml:60 leaves the status unchanged\",\n      \"disposition\": \"fix before merge\",\n      \"findingClass\": \"class-of-bug\",\n      \"scopeProof\": \"the exact-match test is the only membership test at hook-wiring-check.cjs:266; the old reader returned hook-missing for the same command\",\n      \"affectedSurfaceHints\": [\".claude/settings.json UserPromptSubmit command\", \"doctor hook-wiring check\", \"doctor setup status\", \"doctor symlink status\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"remediationWorkstreams\": [\n    {\n      \"order\": 1,\n      \"severity\": \"P1\",\n      \"workstream\": \"Normalize a long node flag to its name before the without-run guard, so the attached value form is rejected as a non-launch; add the attached case to the launch matrix.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"specSeed\": [\n    \"State that the hook-wiring reader treats attached long-flag values (--eval=, --check=) and attached short flags (-e, -p) as non-launches.\"\n  ],\n  \"planSeed\": [\n    \"Test first: add a node --eval=0 <marker> case to tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs expecting exit 1 and hook-missing claude.\",\n    \"Change runsNodeOnMarker to compare flag.split('=')[0] against NODE_FLAGS_WITHOUT_RUN and the argument-taking set.\",\n    \"Rerun node --test on hook-wiring-check.test.cjs and node hook-wiring-check.cjs --root .\"\n  ],\n  \"findingClasses\": [\"class-of-bug\"],\n  \"affectedSurfacesSeed\": [\".claude/settings.json\", \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\", \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml\", \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml\"],\n  \"fixCompletenessRequired\": true\n}\n```\n\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\n\n| ID | Severity | Dimension | File:line | Title | Disposition |\n|----|----------|-----------|-----------|-------|-------------|\n| DR3-P1-001 | P1 | correctness | `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:266` | An attached node evaluation flag still reports the hook as wired | Active, fix before merge |\n\nEvidence for DR3-P1-001: the reader advances over any word starting with `-` and only rejects an exact member of `NODE_FLAGS_WITHOUT_RUN` (`-c`, `--check`, `-e`, `--eval`, `-p`, `--print`, `-v`, `--version`, `-h`, `--help`). `node --eval=0 <marker>` therefore advances to the marker and returns true. The removed `startsCommand` reader returned `hook-missing` for the same command, so the change introduced the false pass. Counterevidence searched: no later guard re-tests the marker as an argument, and no test in `tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs` uses the attached spelling.\n\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\n\n1. **P1, hook-wiring launch reader.** In `runsNodeOnMarker`, split the flag at `=` and test the name against `NODE_FLAGS_WITHOUT_RUN`; do the same for the argument-taking set so `--require=...` and `--conditions=...` advance by one. Add `node --eval=0 <marker>`, `node -e\"1\" <marker>` and `node -p\"1\" <marker>` to the non-launch matrix and keep the existing space-separated cases passing.\n2. **P2 advisories.** None active. Do not re-open the docs, playbook, catalog or baseline work: iterations 2 and 3 verified it against the code and data.\n\n## 5. Spec Seed\n\n- Record the supported launch shapes of the doctor hook-wiring reader as a closed list that includes a quoted script, `env`, `env -u`, `node -r`, `bash/zsh -c`, subshell, brace group, `exec`, background first and a backslash continuation, and record that a node flag carrying its value in the same word is a non-launch.\n- Keep the A10 wording rule: the first count in the detail is verified copies only, and `reported only` covers INFO entries the check did not grade.\n\n## 6. Plan Seed\n\n- One task: attached node flag in the launch reader, with a failing-then-passing test and a rerun of the seven existing launch cases.\n- Out of scope: the four coordinator-left items, the other doctor routes that still carry `<timestamp>` placeholders, and the sealed holdout text.\n\n## 7. Traceability Status\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | pass | T031, T032, T033 match the embed engine and setup workflow; T034, T035, T044 and T045 match the two check scripts; T008 and T018 to T024 and T030 and T043 match their code pages. Only the attached-flag gap in DR3-P1-001 remains. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | CHK-FIX-005 claims the launch matrix and holds every space-separated row; it does not claim the attached flag form, which is the gap DR3-P1-001 names. |\n| `skill_agent` | notApplicable | No agent definition changed. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | notApplicable | No runtime mirror or cross-runtime agent surface changed. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | pass | The three `AdvisorRecommendationSchema` and two `AdvisorRecommendInputSchema` citations resolve; the two include-compiled-route checks exist exactly twice. |\n| `playbook_capability` | pass | The playbook count, no-`NNN-*` rule, no-`CL-002` rule and hand-recorded persistence path all match the tree and the inventory suite. |\n\nAC_COVERAGE: not assessed in this lineage. The dispatch forbids running `validate.sh`, so the advisory signal is left to the root synthesis; this is recorded as a scope limit, not a pass.\n\n## 8. Deferred Items\n\n- The four coordinator-left items in the pass-two tasks.md \"Verifier follow-ups, coordinator\" block stay out of scope by dispatch.\n- The other doctor routes' `<timestamp>` placeholders (`_routes.yaml:72, 99, 506`) are unchanged and outside the changed lines.\n- The `--eval` space-separated form is already rejected; only the attached form is deferred to the P1 workstream.\n- The sealed holdout file was checked by `--numstat` only (0 added, 1 deleted); its prompt text was never read.\n\n## Dimension Expansion Map\n\n- Completed pivots: one per dimension (correctness, then traceability, then maintainability, then security).\n- Failed pivots: none.\n- Audited overrides: none.\n- Swept directions: the changed shell shapes, doctor contracts, doc citations and doc-to-code paths.\n- Remaining frontier: none for this narrow pass.\n\n## 9. Search Ledger\n\n- Correctness: read the complete reader diff, both check scripts, their tests and the removed reader; ran four single-file suites (28, 44, 39, 4 tests, all `fail 0`) and both check binaries.\n- Traceability: read the embed engine's backup naming and restore failure output, the setup workflow, and the two contract suites; confirmed the holdout `--numstat` and the baseline recapture commit.\n- Maintainability: read the six changed prose surfaces and the code each names; ran the playbook suite (2 passed) and the command-bridge field suite (24 passed).\n- Security: walked the doctor assets that call both checks; confirmed neither check executes or interpolates the command string it reads.\n- Ruled out: quoted `echo` scripts, unclosed quotes, `node --check`, space-form `node -e`, comment launches, shell scripts with their own `-c`, `bash -o pipefail -c` (pre-existing), the other routes' `<timestamp>`, the bridge README's optional fields, the playbook path convention, and any execution surface in the changed checks.\n\n## 10. Audit Appendix\n\n- Iterations: 4 of 4, all `complete`; newFindingsRatio 1.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0; convergence reached after the fourth iteration with all four dimensions covered.\n- Findings: 1 new (P1), 0 resolved, 0 repeated.\n- State: every iteration was recorded through `append-mode-event.cjs` (receipts at stream sequences 2 to 5) and the reducer refreshed the registry, dashboard and strategy after each one. `deep-review-state.jsonl` shows exactly four iteration records.\n- Verdict: CONDITIONAL, because DR3-P1-001 stays active and no P0 exists.\n- Scope limit: the dispatch forbids `generate-context.js`, `validate.sh` (including `--recursive`) and every git write, so no continuity save or strict-validation claim is made here; the lineage's completion contract is its own files plus the fan-out completion line.\n- Conflicts recorded: none beyond the validate.sh scope limit above.\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-3/review-report.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-3/review-report.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-3/review-report.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Deep Review Report: doctor-docs-3\\n\\nLineage `doctor-docs-3` of the command-surfacing pass-three fan-out. Session `fanout-doctor-docs-3-1794593402980-zhrui5`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`. Review target `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`, review target type spec-folder. Base commit `ec1869dae8`, head `1ca14a4498`.\\n\\n## 1. Executive Summary\\n\\n- Overall verdict: **CONDITIONAL**\\n- hasAdvisories: false\\n- Active findings: P0 = 0, P1 = 1, P2 = 0\\n- Review scope: the 16 doctor-docs files changed by the two pass-two remediation commits, each read through `git diff ec1869dae8..HEAD`, plus the callers of their changed functions. Pass-one and pass-two findings whose fixes hold are excluded, as are the four coordinator-left items.\\n- Operator review focus: Code review of command surfacing, PASS THREE (narrow). FIRST read the full instructions in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/c9fe91ef-9b85-4bdc-88fb-4d6f766eaecf/scratchpad/review-instructions-3.txt and follow them exactly. Scope file: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/c9fe91ef-9b85-4bdc-88fb-4d6f766eaecf/scratchpad/review-scope-3.txt (area TAB path). Review only the files whose area equals your lineage label without its -3 suffix, by reading git diff ec1869dae8..HEAD for each. Every finding is P0, P1 or P2 with file:line and a concrete input. Never open holdout-prompts.jsonl or read holdout prompt text. Change no code, write only inside your lineage folder.\\n- Four iterations covered correctness, traceability, maintainability and security. The changed doctor contracts, READMEs, playbook, catalog and baseline are clean; the one defect is in the new node-flag reader in the doctor hook-wiring check.\\n\\n## 2. Planning Trigger\\n\\n`/speckit:plan` is required because one active P1 remains. Planning Packet:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"triggered\\\": true,\\n  \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"CONDITIONAL\\\",\\n  \\\"hasAdvisories\\\": false,\\n  \\\"activeFindings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"DR3-P1-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P1\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"An attached node evaluation flag still reports the hook as wired\\\",\\n      \\\"dimension\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:266\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"NODE_FLAGS_WITHOUT_RUN is tested with exact membership on the whole token, so --eval=0, -e\\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\" and -p\\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\" skip the guard; the marker then matches as node's script word\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"node hook-wiring-check.cjs --root . prints ok claude and exits 0 for a command that never runs the marker; doctor-setup.yaml:61 turns that into a PASS delivery leg and doctor-symlink-check.yaml:60 leaves the status unchanged\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"fix before merge\\\",\\n      \\\"findingClass\\\": \\\"class-of-bug\\\",\\n      \\\"scopeProof\\\": \\\"the exact-match test is the only membership test at hook-wiring-check.cjs:266; the old reader returned hook-missing for the same command\\\",\\n      \\\"affectedSurfaceHints\\\": [\\\".claude/settings.json UserPromptSubmit command\\\", \\\"doctor hook-wiring check\\\", \\\"doctor setup status\\\", \\\"doctor symlink status\\\"]\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"remediationWorkstreams\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"order\\\": 1,\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P1\\\",\\n      \\\"workstream\\\": \\\"Normalize a long node flag to its name before the without-run guard, so the attached value form is rejected as a non-launch; add the attached case to the launch matrix.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"specSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\"State that the hook-wiring reader treats attached long-flag values (--eval=, --check=) and attached short flags (-e, -p) as non-launches.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"planSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\"Test first: add a node --eval=0 <marker> case to tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs expecting exit 1 and hook-missing claude.\\\",\\n    \\\"Change runsNodeOnMarker to compare flag.split('=')[0] against NODE_FLAGS_WITHOUT_RUN and the argument-taking set.\\\",\\n    \\\"Rerun node --test on hook-wiring-check.test.cjs and node hook-wiring-check.cjs --root .\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"findingClasses\\\": [\\\"class-of-bug\\\"],\\n  \\\"affectedSurfacesSeed\\\": [\\\".claude/settings.json\\\", \\\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\\\", \\\".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml\\\", \\\".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml\\\"],\\n  \\\"fixCompletenessRequired\\\": true\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\\n\\n| ID | Severity | Dimension | File:line | Title | Disposition |\\n|----|----------|-----------|-----------|-------|-------------|\\n| DR3-P1-001 | P1 | correctness | `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:266` | An attached node evaluation flag still reports the hook as wired | Active, fix before merge |\\n\\nEvidence for DR3-P1-001: the reader advances over any word starting with `-` and only rejects an exact member of `NODE_FLAGS_WITHOUT_RUN` (`-c`, `--check`, `-e`, `--eval`, `-p`, `--print`, `-v`, `--version`, `-h`, `--help`). `node --eval=0 <marker>` therefore advances to the marker and returns true. The removed `startsCommand` reader returned `hook-missing` for the same command, so the change introduced the false pass. Counterevidence searched: no later guard re-tests the marker as an argument, and no test in `tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs` uses the attached spelling.\\n\\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\\n\\n1. **P1, hook-wiring launch reader.** In `runsNodeOnMarker`, split the flag at `=` and test the name against `NODE_FLAGS_WITHOUT_RUN`; do the same for the argument-taking set so `--require=...` and `--conditions=...` advance by one. Add `node --eval=0 <marker>`, `node -e\\\"1\\\" <marker>` and `node -p\\\"1\\\" <marker>` to the non-launch matrix and keep the existing space-separated cases passing.\\n2. **P2 advisories.** None active. Do not re-open the docs, playbook, catalog or baseline work: iterations 2 and 3 verified it against the code and data.\\n\\n## 5. Spec Seed\\n\\n- Record the supported launch shapes of the doctor hook-wiring reader as a closed list that includes a quoted script, `env`, `env -u`, `node -r`, `bash/zsh -c`, subshell, brace group, `exec`, background first and a backslash continuation, and record that a node flag carrying its value in the same word is a non-launch.\\n- Keep the A10 wording rule: the first count in the detail is verified copies only, and `reported only` covers INFO entries the check did not grade.\\n\\n## 6. Plan Seed\\n\\n- One task: attached node flag in the launch reader, with a failing-then-passing test and a rerun of the seven existing launch cases.\\n- Out of scope: the four coordinator-left items, the other doctor routes that still carry `<timestamp>` placeholders, and the sealed holdout text.\\n\\n## 7. Traceability Status\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | pass | T031, T032, T033 match the embed engine and setup workflow; T034, T035, T044 and T045 match the two check scripts; T008 and T018 to T024 and T030 and T043 match their code pages. Only the attached-flag gap in DR3-P1-001 remains. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | CHK-FIX-005 claims the launch matrix and holds every space-separated row; it does not claim the attached flag form, which is the gap DR3-P1-001 names. |\\n| `skill_agent` | notApplicable | No agent definition changed. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | notApplicable | No runtime mirror or cross-runtime agent surface changed. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | pass | The three `AdvisorRecommendationSchema` and two `AdvisorRecommendInputSchema` citations resolve; the two include-compiled-route checks exist exactly twice. |\\n| `playbook_capability` | pass | The playbook count, no-`NNN-*` rule, no-`CL-002` rule and hand-recorded persistence path all match the tree and the inventory suite. |\\n\\nAC_COVERAGE: not assessed in this lineage. The dispatch forbids running `validate.sh`, so the advisory signal is left to the root synthesis; this is recorded as a scope limit, not a pass.\\n\\n## 8. Deferred Items\\n\\n- The four coordinator-left items in the pass-two tasks.md \\\"Verifier follow-ups, coordinator\\\" block stay out of scope by dispatch.\\n- The other doctor routes' `<timestamp>` placeholders (`_routes.yaml:72, 99, 506`) are unchanged and outside the changed lines.\\n- The `--eval` space-separated form is already rejected; only the attached form is deferred to the P1 workstream.\\n- The sealed holdout file was checked by `--numstat` only (0 added, 1 deleted); its prompt text was never read.\\n\\n## Dimension Expansion Map\\n\\n- Completed pivots: one per dimension (correctness, then traceability, then maintainability, then security).\\n- Failed pivots: none.\\n- Audited overrides: none.\\n- Swept directions: the changed shell shapes, doctor contracts, doc citations and doc-to-code paths.\\n- Remaining frontier: none for this narrow pass.\\n\\n## 9. Search Ledger\\n\\n- Correctness: read the complete reader diff, both check scripts, their tests and the removed reader; ran four single-file suites (28, 44, 39, 4 tests, all `fail 0`) and both check binaries.\\n- Traceability: read the embed engine's backup naming and restore failure output, the setup workflow, and the two contract suites; confirmed the holdout `--numstat` and the baseline recapture commit.\\n- Maintainability: read the six changed prose surfaces and the code each names; ran the playbook suite (2 passed) and the command-bridge field suite (24 passed).\\n- Security: walked the doctor assets that call both checks; confirmed neither check executes or interpolates the command string it reads.\\n- Ruled out: quoted `echo` scripts, unclosed quotes, `node --check`, space-form `node -e`, comment launches, shell scripts with their own `-c`, `bash -o pipefail -c` (pre-existing), the other routes' `<timestamp>`, the bridge README's optional fields, the playbook path convention, and any execution surface in the changed checks.\\n\\n## 10. Audit Appendix\\n\\n- Iterations: 4